.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/checklists/cross-layer-drift-gate.md:13:# Cross-layer drift gate — hooks / settings / skills / session metadata need a single explicit gate
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/checklists/cross-layer-drift-gate.md:14:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/checklists/cross-layer-drift-gate.md:15:## What
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/checklists/cross-layer-drift-gate.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/checklists/cross-layer-drift-gate.md:17:Add a single explicit cross-layer consistency gate to the Planning / Execution checklist that verifies the hook script, `settings.json`, the skill docs, and the session schema stay synchronized:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/checklists/cross-layer-drift-gate.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/checklists/cross-layer-drift-gate.md:19:- [ ] Planning: add a cross-layer gate row to the Execution checklist — after T1 + T3 land, run a 4-file consistency check:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/checklists/cross-layer-drift-gate.md:20:  1. `grep -n 'post-tool-use-agents.sh' .claude/settings.json` — verifies both PostToolUse + PostToolUseFailure registrations point to the script
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/checklists/cross-layer-drift-gate.md:21:  2. `grep -n 'worktreePath' .claude/skills/orchestration/SKILL.md` — verifies row 5.5 description is present
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/checklists/cross-layer-drift-gate.md:22:  3. `grep -n 'Your phase:' .claude/skills/delegation/SKILL.md` — verifies structured-header section exists
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/checklists/cross-layer-drift-gate.md:23:  4. `jq '.hooks | keys' .claude/settings.json` — lists all registered hook events
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/checklists/cross-layer-drift-gate.md:24:- [ ] Execution evaluator: include a cross-layer drift check in the Consistency perspective evaluation.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/checklists/cross-layer-drift-gate.md:25:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/checklists/cross-layer-drift-gate.md:26:## Why
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/checklists/cross-layer-drift-gate.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/checklists/cross-layer-drift-gate.md:28:A Risk-perspective evaluator finding from the guardrails Ideation raised this: the guardrails design requires whole-file scans of touched skill files after edits (per `mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md`). However, there is no single explicit cross-layer gate that checks alignment across: `.claude/hooks/post-tool-use-agents.sh`, `.claude/settings.json` (hook registration), `.claude/skills/orchestration/SKILL.md` (worktreePath row description), `.claude/skills/delegation/SKILL.md` (structured-header convention), and `session.template.json` (agents[] schema). These surfaces must stay synchronized; currently each is verified independently.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/checklists/cross-layer-drift-gate.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/checklists/cross-layer-drift-gate.md:30:## Verification
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/checklists/cross-layer-drift-gate.md:31:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/checklists/cross-layer-drift-gate.md:32:The four `grep`/`jq` checks listed under What all pass after T1 + T3 land, and the Execution Consistency-perspective evaluation includes a cross-layer drift check. Concretely: `grep -n 'post-tool-use-agents.sh' .claude/settings.json` returns both registrations, `grep -n 'worktreePath' .claude/skills/orchestration/SKILL.md` returns row 5.5, `grep -n 'Your phase:' .claude/skills/delegation/SKILL.md` returns the structured-header section, and `jq '.hooks | keys' .claude/settings.json` enumerates the registered hook events.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/checklists/cross-layer-drift-gate.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/checklists/cross-layer-drift-gate.md:34:## Status notes
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/checklists/cross-layer-drift-gate.md:35:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/checklists/cross-layer-drift-gate.md:36:Pending. A persistent automated drift detector (e.g., a `gobbi doctor` rule that checks hook registration alignment) is a follow-up beyond this gate. See `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/backlogs/codex-ci-integration-for-dual-system-eval.md` for related automation context.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/checklists/cross-layer-drift-gate.md:37:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/checklists/cross-layer-drift-gate.md:38:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/checklists/cross-layer-drift-gate.md:39:
