.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md:17:# Claude Code PostToolUse + PostToolUseFailure hooks — official schema
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md:19:## Insight
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md:20:PostToolUse fires **after a tool call succeeds**; PostToolUseFailure fires **after a tool call fails**. Both pipe a JSON payload to stdin with these fields:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md:21:- **Common:** `session_id`, `transcript_path`, `cwd`, `permission_mode`, `effort`, `hook_event_name` (= `"PostToolUse"` or `"PostToolUseFailure"`), optional `agent_id` + `agent_type` (populated when the hook fires inside a subagent).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md:22:- **Tool-specific:** `tool_name`, `tool_input` (the input parameters sent to the tool), `tool_use_id` (unique id correlating PreToolUse/PostToolUse pairs), `tool_result` (the result/output; for PostToolUseFailure this carries the failure payload).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md:23:- **Recent additions (v2.1.119+):** `duration_ms` — tool execution time excluding permission prompts / PreToolUse hook execution.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md:25:Matcher patterns support exact string ("Bash"), pipe-separated alternation ("Edit|Write"), regex ("^Notebook"), and MCP-tool patterns ("mcp__memory__.*"). The matcher pattern `"Task"` is the canonical target for hooks that want to fire after subagent spawns.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md:26:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md:27:The hook's `tool_result` payload schema for Task/Agent calls is documented less rigorously than the common fields. The official `tool_result` example in the docs is a simple `{"type": "text", "text": "..."}`. However, the agent-SDK doc (a sibling doc) describes the **TaskOutput** interface as `{result: string, usage?: {input_tokens, output_tokens}, total_cost_usd?, duration_ms?}` for the Task tool. Multiple secondary sources state empirically that "PostToolUse `tool_response` for a completed Agent call carries the subagent's final text along with usage telemetry." Token usage is at least partially observable; the exact shape depends on Claude Code version.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md:28:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md:29:The hook **also receives `transcript_path`** in every fire — meaning a hook can read the transcript JSONL itself and extract the rich `toolUseResult` payload that Claude Code writes (which contains the full subagent metadata: agentId, agentType, totalDurationMs, totalTokens, totalToolUseCount, usage{input_tokens, cache_creation_input_tokens, cache_read_input_tokens, output_tokens}, toolStats{readCount, searchCount, bashCount, editFileCount, linesAdded, linesRemoved}).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md:31:## Related
