.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md:46:> | `PostToolUseFailure`  | After a tool call fails                                                                                                                                |
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md:47:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md:48:**Exit-code behavior table (verbatim):**
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md:49:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md:50:> | Hook event            | Can block? | What happens on exit 2                                                                                               |
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md:51:> | :-------------------- | :--------- | :----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md:52:> | `PostToolUseFailure`  | No         | Shows stderr to Claude (tool already failed)                                                                         |
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md:53:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md:54:Shell-command hook support is explicitly confirmed: PostToolUseFailure supports the same `type: "command"` registration shape as PostToolUse (alongside HTTP, MCP-tool, prompt, and agent hooks). It is non-blocking — exit code 2 does not prevent the underlying tool failure but does surface the hook's stderr to Claude.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md:55:
