.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/backlogs/hook-event-count-31-vs-29-docs-sync.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/backlogs/hook-event-count-31-vs-29-docs-sync.md:21:The session planning artifact for the hook + reconstructor task, and the reference file `features/guardrails/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md`, claim the official hooks page lists 31 hook events. That reference file itself enumerates 29 event names. The current official page visible lifecycle list also shows 29 events. A Codex evaluator independently fetched the page and confirmed 29.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/backlogs/hook-event-count-31-vs-29-docs-sync.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/backlogs/hook-event-count-31-vs-29-docs-sync.md:23:The `PostToolUseFailure` event itself is verified by both Claude and Codex evaluators — this is a supporting-prose defect, not an operational blocker.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/backlogs/hook-event-count-31-vs-29-docs-sync.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/backlogs/hook-event-count-31-vs-29-docs-sync.md:25:## Why deferred
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/backlogs/hook-event-count-31-vs-29-docs-sync.md:26:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/backlogs/hook-event-count-31-vs-29-docs-sync.md:27:Accepted as a non-blocking docs-sync finding at Ideation exit. The load-bearing claim — that `PostToolUseFailure` is a supported shell-command hook event — is independently verified. The count is support prose. Correcting it requires a 2-3 word change in multiple locations and was not worth blocking Planning.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/backlogs/hook-event-count-31-vs-29-docs-sync.md:28:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/guardrails/backlogs/hook-event-count-31-vs-29-docs-sync.md:29:## When to pick up
