.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-convention-deferred-to-planning.md:20:The codex skill stub places `**Constraints**` as a bolded body block after the eighth H2 (`## Anti-patterns`), explicitly annotated as "NOT an H2 section; keeps the H2 count at exactly 8." This preserves the validation contract that `grep -c "^## " .gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/codex/SKILL.md` returns exactly `8`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-convention-deferred-to-planning.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-convention-deferred-to-planning.md:22:A Codex evaluator noted that sampled existing project skills (`execution/SKILL.md`, `wrap-up/SKILL.md`, `research/SKILL.md`) use `## Constraints` as an H2 section, not a body block — raising the question of whether the codex skill should match the sibling-skill convention.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-convention-deferred-to-planning.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-convention-deferred-to-planning.md:24:## Decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-convention-deferred-to-planning.md:25:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-convention-deferred-to-planning.md:26:Keep `**Constraints**` as a body block. The question was deferred from Ideation to the Planning DISCUSSION; at that DISCUSSION the user did not override the locked 8-H2 contract, so the decision stands: the body-block form is the codex-skill-specific pattern, and normalizing `Constraints` across sibling skills is a separate, future session's scope.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-convention-deferred-to-planning.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-convention-deferred-to-planning.md:28:## Rationale
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-convention-deferred-to-planning.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-convention-deferred-to-planning.md:30:The codex skill's locked design enumerates exactly 8 H2 sections and explicitly excludes `Constraints` from them. Promoting `Constraints` to a ninth H2 would break the `grep -c "^## "` returns-8 validation contract that the locked design depends on. Matching the sibling-skill convention is a cosmetic consistency gain that is not worth violating a locked, machine-checked spec mid-stream.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-convention-deferred-to-planning.md:31:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-convention-deferred-to-planning.md:32:## Alternatives considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-convention-deferred-to-planning.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-convention-deferred-to-planning.md:34:- **Promote `Constraints` to a ninth `## Constraints` H2 to match sibling skills** — rejected: violates the locked 8-H2 contract and its grep validation.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-convention-deferred-to-planning.md:35:- **Re-open the 8-H2 lock at Planning DISCUSSION** — offered to the user, who declined to override; the lock was kept.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-convention-deferred-to-planning.md:36:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-convention-deferred-to-planning.md:37:## Consequences
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-convention-deferred-to-planning.md:38:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-convention-deferred-to-planning.md:39:The codex skill keeps the body-block `**Constraints**` form, divergent from sibling skills. A future session may normalize the convention across all skills; until then the divergence is intentional and documented here so it is not mistaken for an oversight.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-convention-deferred-to-planning.md:40:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-convention-deferred-to-planning.md:41:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-convention-deferred-to-planning.md:42:
