.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/eval-fail-revise-escalation.md:13:# Ideation evaluation FAIL — final iteration authorized as a 3-fix surgical revision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/eval-fail-revise-escalation.md:14:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/eval-fail-revise-escalation.md:15:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/eval-fail-revise-escalation.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/eval-fail-revise-escalation.md:17:A round of Ideation evaluation concluded FAIL (Claude returned FAIL; Codex returned REVISE; the pessimistic union is FAIL). The FAIL root cause was that the proposed branch name `session/{date}-{ssid-short}` used an unregistered type prefix `session/` — not present in the `git/conventions.md` branch-type registry. With one evaluation iteration left in the 3-iteration budget, the question was how to spend it.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/eval-fail-revise-escalation.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/eval-fail-revise-escalation.md:19:## Question
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/eval-fail-revise-escalation.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/eval-fail-revise-escalation.md:21:Given the FAIL, how should the final allowed evaluation iteration proceed — a broad re-work, or a narrow targeted fix?
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/eval-fail-revise-escalation.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/eval-fail-revise-escalation.md:23:## Options considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/eval-fail-revise-escalation.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/eval-fail-revise-escalation.md:25:- **Surgical 3-fix revision** — change only the three items tied to the FAIL findings, no other content changes, and re-evaluate.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/eval-fail-revise-escalation.md:26:- **Broader re-work of the Ideation design** — reopen more of the design, risking new findings late in the budget with no iterations left to absorb them.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/eval-fail-revise-escalation.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/eval-fail-revise-escalation.md:28:## User decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/eval-fail-revise-escalation.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/eval-fail-revise-escalation.md:30:The user authorized a surgical 3-fix revision, with no other content changes:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/eval-fail-revise-escalation.md:31:1. **Fix A**: replace `session/{date}-{ssid-short}` with `chore/session-{date}-{ssid-short}` everywhere — a user-locked branch prefix reusing the already-registered `chore` type.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/eval-fail-revise-escalation.md:32:2. **Fix B**: verify the `PostToolUseFailure` hook event officially via WebFetch of `https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks` and preserve the verbatim quote.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/eval-fail-revise-escalation.md:33:3. **Fix C**: flag the `.gobbi/project.json` initialization step in the project-json resolver design as a dormant precondition and stage a feature-level backlog item for it.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/eval-fail-revise-escalation.md:34:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/eval-fail-revise-escalation.md:35:This was the final iteration allowed under the 3-iteration evaluation budget.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/eval-fail-revise-escalation.md:36:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/eval-fail-revise-escalation.md:37:## Implication
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/eval-fail-revise-escalation.md:38:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/eval-fail-revise-escalation.md:39:All active design statements were updated to the `chore/session-` prefix; the verbatim `PostToolUseFailure` quote was preserved; and the dormant `.gobbi/project.json` precondition was documented in the project-json resolver design. The `chore/session-` branch prefix is now the user-locked convention (this worktree's branch follows it).
