.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/changelogs/2026-05-26-bundle-c-rehome.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/changelogs/2026-05-26-bundle-c-rehome.md:18:## Summary
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/changelogs/2026-05-26-bundle-c-rehome.md:19:Bundle C was a work-sprint, not a value-feature. Its durable in-dir artifacts were the 5 files documenting the `gobbi-hook-authoring` skill: one shipped-changelog and four evaluation checklists (quality gates for the skill). Per design §1.3 row 4 + §8 LOW-16 routing heuristic rule 1 (destination = the capability the CONTENT is about), all five route to `install-runtime` — the value-feature that owns the `gobbi-hook-authoring` skill (design §10 RATIFY-1). Files moved via `git mv` (history-preserving); the changelog's `feature:` frontmatter restamped to `install-runtime`. Bodies unchanged.
