.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:16:# Do not promote a third backlog for the triplicate dangling-claude-skill-link entries
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:18:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:20:During Preparation readiness scanning (iter 1), the draft described the dangling `[claude skill](skills/claude/SKILL.md)` link at `.claude/CLAUDE.md:60` as "1 new gap found this loop" and staged a third backlog record at `preparation/staging/backlogs/project/dangling-claude-doc-skill-link.md` (priority LOW, disposition deferred).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:22:Dual-system evaluation (Claude: Project/Risk/Usage perspectives; Overall) confirmed that two committed backlog files already track this exact issue at HEAD `d2b5b37`:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:23:- `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/backlogs/claude-doc-standard-skill-missing.md` (FLAG-2, priority HIGH, disposition open, created 2026-05-25)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:24:- `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/backlogs/stub-redirect-dangling-claude-skill-ref.md` (FLAG-3, priority MEDIUM, disposition open)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:25:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:26:Both confirmed present via `git cat-file -e HEAD:...` and counted inside the 208-doc P_live_all population. The staged third record was a semantic duplicate with a different slug and conflicting priority (LOW) that would have created three active records for one concept at Wrap-up — violating one-record-one-concept atomicity (rules.md §3).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:28:The Claude evaluator also noted (F4/Risk) that this is a near-recurrence of the "did-not-check-existing-tracked-files" failure mode — the loop scanned the 208-doc population but did not check whether the gap was already recorded as a committed backlog.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:30:## Decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:31:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:32:Do NOT promote the third staged backlog. The redundant file `preparation/staging/backlogs/project/dangling-claude-doc-skill-link.md` was DELETED during MEMORIZATION (session staging, pre-promotion — the never-delete rule does not apply to session scratch). The existing FLAG-2 (HIGH, open) and FLAG-3 (MEDIUM, open) backlog files are untouched and remain authoritative.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:34:## Rationale
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:35:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:36:- Promoting a third record with conflicting priority (LOW vs existing HIGH/MEDIUM) would defeat backlog triage and violate one-record-one-concept atomicity per rules.md §3.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:37:- The existing FLAG-2 HIGH classification is the maintainer's original calibration and remains the standing priority.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:38:- The Wrap-up literal-slug check alone is insufficient to prevent semantic duplicates — this decision captures the gap explicitly so Wrap-up knows not to promote.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:39:- This is also a mistake-candidate for the project: the Preparation loop scanned the population count (208) but did not cross-check whether the surfaced gap was already present as a committed backlog entry. See note below.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:40:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:41:## Alternatives considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:42:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:43:1. **Supersede FLAG-2/FLAG-3 into one canonical record** — not pursued; that is a separate dedicated cleanup, not in scope for this retrofit session.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:44:2. **Update the draft to cross-link FLAG-2/FLAG-3** — partial; the decision record here serves that purpose without mutating the rawdata draft post-evaluation.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:45:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:46:## Consequences
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:47:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:48:- Wrap-up MUST NOT promote `dangling-claude-doc-skill-link.md` (it no longer exists in staging).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:49:- Wrap-up reads this decision record to confirm the item was already tracked.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:50:- FLAG-2/FLAG-3 remain the live records; no priority reconciliation performed in this session.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:51:- A mistake-candidate for "population-scan-without-committed-backlog-cross-check" may be warranted at Wrap-up.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:52:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/triplicate-backlog-remediated.md:53:## Related
