.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:14:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:16:# Codex skill — assistant-wrapper pattern for dual-system evaluation
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:18:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:20:Dual-system evaluation runs a Claude evaluator and a Codex evaluator in parallel over the same artifact. Three failure modes were observed when the manager tried to drive the Codex side directly:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:22:1. **`codex:codex-rescue` plugin agent fire-and-forget**: the plugin agent forwarded the task to the companion runtime, returned immediately with placeholder text, and the output files were never written.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:23:2. **`codex exec` sandbox project-root detection**: codex auto-detected the wrong project root for absolute session paths and rejected writes with "writing outside of the project"; it required `--cd /playinganalytics/git/gobbi --add-dir <session-path>` flags to write where intended.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:24:3. **`codex exec` background Bash + notification timing**: codex completed successfully (exit 0, all output files written), but the Claude Code harness delivered the completion notification only embedded in the manager's next tool-call result, so the manager could not reliably await it.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:25:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:26:## Decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:28:The codex skill documents the **assistant-wrapper pattern** as the recommended topology for dual-system parallel evaluation:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:30:1. The manager spawns 2 `assistant` subagents in parallel via `Agent(subagent_type="assistant", run_in_background: true, ...)`, one Claude-side and one Codex-side.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:31:2. The Codex-side assistant's prompt instructs it to run `codex exec --sandbox workspace-write --cd <main-tree> --add-dir <session-path>` via its own internal Bash tool, **foreground** (no `run_in_background` inside the subagent).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:32:3. The Codex-side assistant's Bash blocks synchronously until codex exits; the assistant reads codex stdout, verifies output files were written at the contracted paths, re-greps for required content, and only then reports DONE.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:33:4. The Claude-side assistant runs its evaluation via its own Bash/Read tools normally.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:34:5. Each assistant returns via Agent completion notification (background topology).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:35:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:36:## Rationale
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:37:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:38:The wrapper closes every failure surface that the direct paths leave open: the assistant body explicitly awaits codex via a foreground Bash and validates the written files before reporting, so fire-and-forget, notification delay, and silent sandbox rejections all surface as a failed validation rather than a false DONE.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:39:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:40:## Alternatives considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:41:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:42:| Rejected pattern | Failure surface | Why the wrapper wins |
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:43:|---|---|---|
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:44:| `Agent(codex:codex-rescue, ...)` | Fire-and-forget, no await | Assistant body explicitly awaits via Bash + validates |
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:45:| Manager-direct `Bash(codex exec, run_in_background: true)` | Notification delay; raw stdout; no validation | Assistant validates files-written, re-greps, reports verified DONE |
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:46:| Manager-direct `Bash(codex exec, run_in_background: false)` | Blocks the manager; no parallelism | Assistant background gives parallelism + validation |
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:47:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:48:## Consequences
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:49:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:50:The codex skill carries the assistant-wrapper pattern as the canonical dual-system evaluator spawn topology; manager-direct codex invocation for evaluation is documented as an anti-pattern.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:51:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:52:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:53:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-skill-assistant-wrapper-pattern-for-dual-system-eval.md:54:- Shipped in commit `b9970dc` — `codex/SKILL.md § Use cases § Dual-system evaluator spawn`.
