.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/fx1-sub-count-cross-foot.md:16:# FIX-1 backlog-disposition sub-count cross-foot (28 vs 27) — normalize to the strict figure
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/fx1-sub-count-cross-foot.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/fx1-sub-count-cross-foot.md:18:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/fx1-sub-count-cross-foot.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/fx1-sub-count-cross-foot.md:20:The Preparation readiness work used "28 backlog disposition files legitimate (preserved)" in one place and "27" (strict P_live filter) in two others, labelling the discrepancy a cosmetic note. A Consistency-perspective re-run confirmed the strict figure is 27.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/fx1-sub-count-cross-foot.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/fx1-sub-count-cross-foot.md:22:Both numbers appeared in the same readiness artifact without reconciliation, creating a self-inconsistent reference that would carry forward into Planning.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/fx1-sub-count-cross-foot.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/fx1-sub-count-cross-foot.md:24:## Decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/fx1-sub-count-cross-foot.md:25:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/fx1-sub-count-cross-foot.md:26:Deferred to Execution: the standard-authoring wave normalizes the canonical figure to 27 (strict P_live filter) and footnotes or removes the loose-filter 28. Planning uses 27 as the canonical backlog-disposition sub-count.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/fx1-sub-count-cross-foot.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/fx1-sub-count-cross-foot.md:28:## Rationale
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/fx1-sub-count-cross-foot.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/fx1-sub-count-cross-foot.md:30:This is a documented cosmetic discrepancy, not a baseline error. The strict-filter figure (27) is reproducible; the loose-filter figure (28) was already flagged for normalization. Neither readiness nor the leak baseline depends on which figure is cited.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/fx1-sub-count-cross-foot.md:31:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/fx1-sub-count-cross-foot.md:32:## Alternatives considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/fx1-sub-count-cross-foot.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/fx1-sub-count-cross-foot.md:34:Reconcile the two figures inline in the originating readiness draft — rejected: that draft is read-only audit rawdata; the canonical figure is fixed downstream at Execution instead.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/fx1-sub-count-cross-foot.md:35:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/fx1-sub-count-cross-foot.md:36:## Consequences
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/fx1-sub-count-cross-foot.md:37:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/fx1-sub-count-cross-foot.md:38:Execution states the backlog-disposition count once, using the strict P_live filter (27), and does not mix filters in a single count narrative. The discrepancy does not affect the FIX-1 predicate or the leak-file set.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/fx1-sub-count-cross-foot.md:39:
