.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:17:# 5-Type Finding Vocabulary
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:19:## Insight
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:21:Evaluation findings are classified into exactly five types, and that closed vocabulary is what every evaluation-staging file's frontmatter must use verbatim:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:23:```
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:24:scenario_gap      — A scenario exists in project memory but no checklist item or task covers it.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:25:checklist_gap     — A checklist item exists but no task implements or verifies it.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:26:design_flaw       — A structural or design problem in the artifact under evaluation.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:27:assumption_risk   — An assumption in the artifact that may not hold at execution time.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:28:general           — A finding that does not fit the four above categories.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:29:```
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:31:The split that matters operationally is mechanical-class vs judgment-required:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:32:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:33:- **Mechanical-class** (auto-backfill via Step 2.5): `scenario_gap`, `checklist_gap`, `general`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:34:- **Judgment-required** (trigger NEEDS_CONTEXT): `design_flaw`, `assumption_risk`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:35:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:36:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:37:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:38:- [`design/naming-convention-enforcement.md`](../design/naming-convention-enforcement.md) — the Coverage Ownership Matrix row that has the Consistency + Aesthetics perspectives verify this 5-Type vocabulary appears correctly in staging frontmatter.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:39:- [`decisions/coverage-ownership-matrix-row-text.md`](../decisions/coverage-ownership-matrix-row-text.md) — fixes the matrix-cell wording that cites this vocabulary.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:40:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:41:## Why it applies
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:42:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:43:Any Execution task that authors evaluation skill content, or any agent that stages an evaluation finding, must use these exact type strings — an invented or misspelled type breaks the mechanical-vs-judgment routing and the staging-shape checks. Invoke this reference whenever writing or reviewing finding frontmatter.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/references/five-type-vocabulary.md:44:
