.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:14:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:16:# Codex skill invocation priority
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:18:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:20:The codex skill can be invoked two ways: by running the `codex exec` CLI command through the Bash tool, or by spawning a Codex plugin agent (`codex:codex-rescue`) through the Agent tool. The design had to fix which of these is the primary invocation pattern across every role (manager and subagents), and whether subagents are even able to use the plugin-agent path — the user recalled "some blocks" but could not name them.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:22:## Decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:24:`codex exec` via Bash is the UNIVERSAL primary invocation pattern — for the manager and for every subagent alike. The Codex plugin agent (`codex:codex-rescue`) is a manager-only secondary path, and the `/codex:adversarial-review` slash command is a user-only tertiary path.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:25:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:26:## Rationale
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:28:The user's direction was: "I think it's better for subagents to use codex cli command like 'codex exec'. Manager too. I think we need to check if subagents can use codex plugin skills. I remember there were some blocks." A manager investigation confirmed why the CLI path must be universal:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:30:- `.claude/agents/{leader,executor,evaluator,assistant}.md` tool surfaces — NONE include the Agent tool. Subagents therefore cannot spawn the `codex:codex-rescue` plugin agent at all. This is the "block" the user remembered.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:31:- `.claude/agents/manager.md` has `tools: "*"` — only the manager can spawn `codex:codex-rescue`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:32:- `~/.claude/plugins/cache/openai-codex/codex/1.0.2/agents/codex-rescue.md` is itself `tools: Bash` — even the plugin agent is a thin Bash wrapper around `codex exec`, so the CLI is the lowest common denominator anyway.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:33:- `codex-cli 0.133.0` is installed at `/home/jeonhh0061/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.1/bin/codex`; `codex exec` supports `--cd`, `--add-dir`, sandbox modes, and `-c` config overrides — enough to cover every role's needs.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:34:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:35:## Alternatives considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:36:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:37:- **Plugin agent (`codex:codex-rescue`) as the primary pattern** — rejected: subagents lack the Agent tool and cannot spawn it, so a plugin-first design would leave every subagent without a Codex path.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:38:- **Treat the two paths as equal** — rejected: equality forces every caller to branch on its own role; making the CLI universal removes that branching and keeps the plugin agent as a manager-only convenience.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:39:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:40:## Consequences
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:41:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:42:The codex skill is specced so that:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:43:1. **Primary pattern (universal — manager AND subagents)**: `codex exec` via Bash.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:44:2. **Secondary pattern (manager-only)**: `Agent(subagent_type="codex:codex-rescue", ...)` for ad-hoc rescue / second-opinion work.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:45:3. **Anti-pattern**: trying to spawn a Codex plugin agent from a subagent context.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:46:4. **User-action pattern**: `/codex:adversarial-review` is `disable-model-invocation: true` — neither manager nor subagent can invoke it.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:47:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:48:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:49:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:50:- This decision was split out from a bundled user-redirect record; the full originating session narrative is preserved in [`features/workflow/archive/decisions/2026-05-23-iter1-user-redirects.md`](../../workflow/archive/decisions/2026-05-23-iter1-user-redirects.md).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:51:- [`discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md`](../discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md) — the AskUserQuestion exchange that set this direction.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md:52:- [`design/codex-skill-structure.md`](../design/codex-skill-structure.md) — the skill structure this invocation priority feeds into.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:1:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:2:name: constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:3:description: Keep the Constraints body block in the codex skill — the 8-H2 Idea Design A contract takes precedence over the H2-per-section convention used by sibling skills.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:4:type: decisions
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:5:scope: feature
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:6:feature: evaluation
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:7:status: active
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:8:created: 2026-05-23
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:9:session: 2026-05-23-7ea62d36-e826-4ce6-9e90-9e948007b068
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:10:tags: [codex, constraints, h2-count, codex-skill]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:11:supersedes: null
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:12:superseded_by: null
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:13:decision_status: accepted
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:14:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:16:# Constraints body block vs ## Constraints H2 convention
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:18:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:20:The codex skill stub renders `Constraints` as a bolded `**Constraints**` body block rather than a `## Constraints` H2, to keep the skill at exactly 8 H2 sections. Sampled existing project skills use `## Constraints` as an H2, which raised two questions: should the codex stub be revved to a ninth H2 to match, and the stub's annotation cited `_claude/SKILL.md` as the convention source — is that citation correct?
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:22:## Decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:24:Keep the `**Constraints**` body block, and drop the `_claude/SKILL.md` citation. The annotation is changed to read "body block per locked Idea Design A; H2 count contract" instead of pointing at a non-existent skill file.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:25:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:26:## Rationale
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:28:The codex skill's locked design fixed exactly 8 H2 sections — the contract `grep -c "^## " SKILL.md` MUST return 8 — so a ninth `## Constraints` H2 would break the lock. Two pieces of evidence settled the rest:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:30:- **6/6 sampled skills use `## Constraints` as H2.** `grep -n "^## Constraints" .agents/skills/*/SKILL.md` confirms git, research, preparation, wrap-up, mistake, and execution all use the H2 form — so the divergence is real, but it does not justify breaking the locked 8-H2 count.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:31:- **`_claude/SKILL.md` does not exist.** `find /playinganalytics/git/gobbi -path "*/skills/claude*" -type f` finds only symlinks to other skills — neither `.agents/skills/_claude/` nor `.claude/skills/claude/` exists. The stub's citation pointed at a phantom file, so it had to be replaced.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:32:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:33:## Alternatives considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:34:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:35:- **Rev the stub to a ninth `## Constraints` H2 to match the 6 sibling skills** — rejected: breaks the locked 8-H2 grep contract.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:36:- **Keep the `_claude/SKILL.md` citation** — rejected: the file does not exist, so the citation is a dangling reference; it was replaced with a citation to the locked Idea Design A and the H2-count contract.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:37:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:38:## Consequences
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:39:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:40:The codex skill keeps the body-block form, divergent from the 6 H2-form sibling skills, and its Constraints annotation now cites a real source (the locked design + H2 contract). The decision was adopted directly into the codex-skill stub-authoring brief with no user challenge.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:41:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:42:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:43:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:44:- [`decisions/constraints-body-block-convention-deferred-to-planning.md`](constraints-body-block-convention-deferred-to-planning.md) — the deferral decision this one resolves.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/decisions/constraints-body-block-kept-per-h2-lock.md:45:- [`design/codex-skill-structure.md`](../design/codex-skill-structure.md) — the locked design that fixes the 8-H2 contract.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:1:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:2:name: codex-invocation-priority-redirect
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:3:description: User confirmed codex exec via Bash as the universal primary invocation pattern for all roles; manager empirical investigation revealed subagents cannot spawn plugin agents.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:4:type: discussions
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:5:scope: feature
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:6:feature: evaluation
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:7:status: active
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:8:created: 2026-05-23
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:9:session: 2026-05-23-7ea62d36-e826-4ce6-9e90-9e948007b068
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:10:tags: [codex, invocation, subagents, plugin-agents]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:11:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:12:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:13:# Codex Invocation Priority
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:14:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:15:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:17:The codex skill design had two candidate invocation paths — the `codex exec` CLI command via Bash, and the `codex:codex-rescue` plugin agent via the Agent tool — and needed to fix which is primary across roles. The user recalled "some blocks" on subagents using Codex plugin skills but could not name them, so the priority could not be settled without resolving that open question first.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:19:## Question
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:21:In the codex skill design, which Codex invocation pattern should be the primary one — plugin agent first, `codex exec` first, or treated as equal?
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:23:## Options considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:25:- **`codex exec` first (universal)** — every role, manager and subagent alike, invokes Codex through the CLI; the plugin agent is a secondary convenience.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:26:- **Plugin agent first** — `codex:codex-rescue` is the primary path, falling back to the CLI.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:27:- **Treat both as equal** — no fixed priority; each caller picks.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:28:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:29:## User decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:31:The user chose CLI-first: "I think it's better for subagents to use codex cli command like 'codex exec'. Manager too. I think we need to check if subagents can use codex plugin skills. I remember there were some blocks." A manager investigation then resolved the "blocks" the user remembered:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:32:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:33:- `.claude/agents/{leader,executor,evaluator,assistant}.md` all lack the Agent tool — subagents cannot spawn the `codex:codex-rescue` plugin agent.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:34:- `.claude/agents/manager.md` has `tools: "*"` — only the manager can spawn plugin agents.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:35:- The plugin agent (`agents/codex-rescue.md`) itself declares `tools: Bash` — it is a thin Bash wrapper around `codex exec`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:36:- The remembered "blocks" = subagents cannot spawn plugin agents because they lack the Agent tool.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:37:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:38:## Implication
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:39:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:40:`codex exec` via Bash is the UNIVERSAL primary pattern (manager AND subagents); `codex:codex-rescue` is a manager-only secondary path; `/codex:adversarial-review` is a user-only tertiary path. The codex skill's invocation-patterns section was reordered accordingly, and a new subsection "Why subagents must use `codex exec`" was added carrying the empirical tool-surface witness.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:41:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:42:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:43:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:44:- [`decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md`](../decisions/codex-exec-universal-invocation-pattern.md) — the decision record this discussion produced.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/discussions/codex-invocation-priority-redirect.md:45:- [`design/codex-skill-structure.md`](../design/codex-skill-structure.md) — the skill structure whose invocation-patterns section encodes this priority.
