.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:12:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:13:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:14:# Preparation Loop — Readiness Decision (env-var audit + SessionStart hook)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:16:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:18:Before the env-var-audit + SessionStart-hook feature could advance from Preparation to Planning, its readiness artifact had to clear a dual-system evaluation gate. The first evaluation round returned REVISE from both Claude and Codex; this decision records the readiness verdict, the findings that drove it, and their dispositions.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:20:## Decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:22:**The Preparation loop is PASS — the feature is ready to advance to Planning.** The first round returned REVISE/REVISE; after the accepted remediations were applied, the second round returned PASS/PASS.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:24:| Round | Claude verdict | Codex verdict | Outcome |
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:25:|------|---------------|---------------|---------|
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:26:| 1 | REVISE | REVISE | Remediation applied |
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:27:| 2 | PASS | PASS | Advance to Planning |
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:28:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:29:## Rationale
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:31:Three findings from the first round were accepted and remediated in the second round:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:32:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:33:- **Finding α — Branch name (`feature/` → `feat/`), High (convention violation).** The artifact used `feature/env-var-audit-sessionstart-hook` as the suggested branch name. `git/conventions.md` Step-1 regex requires `feat/` and explicitly lists `feature/oauth` as the FAIL example. Disposition: accepted; `feature/` replaced with `feat/` at the two pre-planning locations. Historical references in the changelog description were preserved as-is.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:34:- **Finding β — `jq -e` two-step verification, High (incorrect verification command).** The single `jq -e '.transcriptPath' ...` command cannot distinguish present-with-null from absent; `jq -e` exits nonzero on `null` and `false`, so the check would false-fail on a correctly-set null value. Disposition: accepted; replaced with a two-step verification — `jq -e 'has("transcriptPath")'` for presence, then plain `jq '.transcriptPath'` for value, with an inline note that the two steps are needed because `jq -e` returns nonzero on null.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:35:- **Finding γ — Main-tree absolute session-write path note, Medium (missing Planning/Execution guard).** The artifact lacked an explicit reminder that all session writes (session.json stamping, staging files, mistake notes) must use the main-tree absolute path, not the executor's worktree path. Disposition: accepted; added pre-planning item 10 "Session-write path discipline (main-tree absolute)" with authority citations (`git/SKILL.md:31-33` Memory Access Matrix + `git/SKILL.md:276` Output paths).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:36:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:37:## Alternatives considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:38:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:39:- **Finding δ — `gh auth` dispute (Codex filed High).** The Codex evaluator reported the active `HahyeonJeon` token as invalid, challenging the §3 "tooling verified" exit criterion. Disposition: **disputed as an environment mismatch, not accepted.** The manager independently re-ran `gh auth status` in the main session shell and received a valid, active login ("Logged in to github.com account HahyeonJeon, Active account: true, Token scopes: admin:public_key, gist, read:org, repo"). The Codex sandbox subprocess lacked auth credentials — a runtime artifact of the sandbox, not a real Preparation gap. No code change applied; mitigation is that the manager re-verifies `gh auth status` at point of use if Execution subagents shell out to `gh`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:40:- **Two carry-forward deferred items (Low; do not block Planning).** (1) A stale `rg` version claim — the artifact cites `rg` 14.1.1; the actual installed version may differ, but Planning re-greps at point of use regardless. (2) An absent-vs-empty staging-subdir wording imprecision — cosmetic; does not affect Planning or Execution. Both were judged pre-existing/cosmetic and deferred rather than fixed.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:41:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:42:## Consequences
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:43:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:44:- The feature advances to Planning with the three accepted remediations baked into the readiness artifact.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:45:- The `gh auth` re-verification mitigation carries into Execution: the manager re-checks `gh auth status` at point of use before any subagent shells out to `gh`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:46:- The two deferred items remain open as low-priority cosmetics; neither blocks Planning or Execution.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:47:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/pre-planning-readiness-decisions.md:48:## Related
