.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/README.md:16:Dual-system review (Claude + Codex) across 7 perspectives, gating each deliverable before acceptance. This is value-feature #4 of the 7 capability features defined in the memory-system redesign.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/README.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/README.md:18:## Overview
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/README.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/README.md:20:`evaluation` is gobbi's review subsystem: a 4-stage procedure run by two independent systems (Claude + Codex) across 7 perspectives plus Overall, with finding metadata and cross-system reconciliation, gating each deliverable before it is accepted.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/README.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/README.md:22:## Status
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/README.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/README.md:24:Active. The dual-system evaluation procedure, the 7-perspective set, the 5-Type finding vocabulary, and the codex-invocation conventions are shipped and in use. The feature directory was created during the memory-system redesign (W3-T0) and the codex / dual-system-evaluation artifacts from the Bundle A and Bundle B sprints have been re-homed here.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/README.md:25:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/README.md:26:## Subsystems
