.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/README.md:17:# Feature: Project Memory
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/README.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/README.md:19:Cross-session durable store: decisions, designs, plans, and references survive in a typed, searchable memory tree. This is value-feature #2 of the 7 capability features (design §1.2, RATIFY-1 / L1). The memory-system redesign lands here.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/README.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/README.md:21:## Overview
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/README.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/README.md:23:`project-memory` is gobbi's durable cross-session knowledge tree. It captures what survives a session — decisions, designs, plans, references, mistakes — in a typed, named, frontmattered store that the next session can find without restarting from zero.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/README.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/README.md:25:## Status
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/README.md:26:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/README.md:27:Active. The memory-system redesign shipped the typed directory structure and naming standard (PR #272), and the dev-doc quality standard (§4 of `memorization/rules.md`) plus a conformance wave shipped on top of it. The prose-quality wave that brings each doc into full §4 conformance is in progress. The subsystems this feature owns — `memorization` (synthesis + staging), `wrap-up`'s promotion half, the project-memory types + naming + frontmatter standards, and the archive move-on-terminal model — are all live.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/README.md:28:
