.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:19:# Design — development-document-level project-memory standard
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:21:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:23:PR #272 fixed where memory files live and what they are named. It did NOT define or enforce
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:24:how well each doc is written as a development document. Two evidenced consequences (HEAD d2b5b37):
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:25:1. Frontmatter never retrofitted: 50 / 208 live docs carry the full base schema (~24%).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:26:2. Cryptic session-internal references survive in doc bodies (confirmed at
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:27:   `features/git-workflow/design/worktree-create-before-session-stamp.md:31-33,49-51`).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:28:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:29:The work is scoped into three tiers, in priority order:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:30:- Tier 1 (primary): write the dev-doc standard as a new section in `memorization/rules.md`;
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:31:  run conformance wave (mechanical, type-aware FIX-1 strip + base-schema normalization);
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:32:  run prose-quality wave (per-type rewrite).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:33:- Tier 2 (optional): minimal mechanical grep gate extended to `features/` (verification
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:34:  command only; no behavioral change; heavier enforcement deferred).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:35:- Tier 3 (tertiary): light nav wave — verify each feature README.md's Subdirectories section.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:36:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:37:Explicitly out-of-scope: re-home, big-bang rewrite, new eval perspective, Principle-13 surgery,
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:38:frozen archive/ docs, stripping legitimate per-type frontmatter keys.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:39:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:40:## Approach
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:41:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:42:### Standard authoring (wave 0 — the spec)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:43:A new section is added to `memorization/rules.md` (canonical:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:44:`.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/memorization/rules.md`). The section:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:45:- Defines a dev-doc (a doc a zero-context reader understands end-to-end).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:46:- Leads with "what good looks like" + a real before/after table drawn from this tree.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:47:- Specifies per-type section contracts:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:48:  - decisions/design → Context → Decision → Rationale → Alternatives → Consequences → Related (ADR-shaped).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:49:  - mistakes → What/Why/Recognize/Corrected (existing enforced schema).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:50:  - learnings → Insight → Context → Why-it-matters → How-to-apply → Counter-cases.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:51:  - notes → What-happened → What-shipped → Deferred → Decisions-to-respect.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:52:- States the self-contained-prose rule: no load-bearing vanished-session coordinates in bodies.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:53:- States the type-purity rule (per Diátaxis): one doc, one type's job; do not blend types.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:54:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:55:### Conformance wave (wave 1 — mechanical)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:56:Apply the FIX-1 type-aware allowlist strip (see [type-aware-strip-disposition-not-blanket-leak](../decisions/type-aware-strip-disposition-not-blanket-leak.md) for the full predicate).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:57:Also normalize base schema (add missing base keys) and de-crypt cryptic session-coord body
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:58:references. Absorb backlog `feature-dir-frontmatter-full-normalization.md`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:59:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:60:### Prose-quality wave (wave 2 — per type)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:61:Rewrite bodies toward the quality bar, type-by-type. Verify per wave.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:62:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:63:### Tier-3 nav wave (wave 3 — light, lowest priority)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:64:Verify each feature README.md's Subdirectories section; optionally add top-level index pointer.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:65:Must not block tier-1.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:66:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:67:## Rationale
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:68:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:69:The standard optimizes for durable, machine-addressable project memory that a zero-context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:70:reader can navigate without re-reading session transcripts. The wave-based sequencing (spec →
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:71:mechanical conformance → per-type prose → light nav) honors the steel-man's anti-big-bang
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:72:warning while staying bottom-up: each wave is independently verifiable before the next begins.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:73:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:74:**The scenarios the standard must serve** (the teaching examples that motivate the section
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:75:contracts):
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:76:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:77:- **Golden path:** a new `decisions/` doc authored next session passes type-purity + ADR section
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:78:  contract + base frontmatter + self-contained-prose checks with zero rework.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:79:- **Edge (legitimate-key backlog):** a `backlogs/` doc with both legitimate `disposition` AND
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:80:  illegitimate eval-routing keys — the FIX-1 predicate strips the eval keys, preserves `disposition`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:81:- **Edge (half-narrative):** a migrated design doc with `T1-I-2` / `draft-iter3.md:308` in the
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:82:  body — retrofit keeps the decision prose, lifts provenance to frontmatter/footer, drops inline
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:83:  coordinates.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:84:- **Failure (no clear home):** a session-journal mislabeled as `design/` — reclassify to `notes/`;
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:85:  never delete.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:86:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:87:**How each wave is validated** (the evidence that the approach worked):
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:88:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:89:- Standard section exists in canonical `rules.md`; symlink auto-reflects.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:90:- Conformance wave: type-aware grep gate reports 0 illegitimate keys; 100% P_live_all (208) carry
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:91:  base schema.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:92:- Prose wave: evaluator scores 3 sample docs against the section-contract checklist — pass/fail.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:93:- Nav wave: each feature README.md Subdirectories section lists all existing subdirs.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:94:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:95:## Alternatives considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:96:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:97:- **Big-bang rewrite** — rejected: a one-shot rewrite of all 208 docs is faster on paper but
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:98:  fails opaquely under context pressure (Principle 3) and forfeits per-wave verification. The
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:99:  wave-based approach is slower than big-bang but de-risked, and it honors the steel-man's
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:100:  explicit anti-big-bang warning.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:101:- **Blanket grep strip of frontmatter keys** — rejected in favor of the type-aware FIX-1
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:102:  allowlist, which preserves keys legitimate for a doc's type (e.g., `disposition` on a
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:103:  `backlogs/` doc) instead of stripping every routing-shaped key indiscriminately.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:104:- **Deleting mislabeled narrative** — rejected: a session-journal mislabeled as `design/` is
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:105:  reclassified to `notes/`, never deleted; deleting valuable history to satisfy type-purity
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:106:  would trade one defect for another.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:107:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:108:## Consequences
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:109:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:110:- The standard lives as a new section in canonical `rules.md`; the symlink auto-reflects it, so
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:111:  every agent loading memorization meets the same contract.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:112:- Conformance and prose are enforced per wave, not in one pass — slower throughput, higher
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:113:  confidence, and a clean intervention point between waves.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:114:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:115:Forward-consequences carried as open issues for Execution:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:116:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:117:- **CN-1 (Low, cosmetic):** FIX-1 disposition sub-count cross-foot (28 vs 27 under strict filter).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:118:  Normalize at Execution.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:119:- **PR-1 (Low, confirm/defer):** AGENTS.md 12→13 entrypoint reconciliation — surface at Planning.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:120:- **12/13/16 type-count framing:** when authoring the standard's per-type section list, reconcile
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:121:  against `rules.md` §2 (12 promotable + 4 feature-subdir-only = 16) and `memory-map.md` (13 types).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:122:  Not a blocker; a standard-authoring concern for Execution.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:123:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:124:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:125:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/design/dev-doc-memory-standard.md:126:- [`skills/memorization/rules.md`](../../../skills/memorization/rules.md)
