.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/scenarios/tier-2-3-scope-explicitly-placed.md:28:- The user's ratified three-tier scope: "Cover all three; priority = (1) standard + content
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/scenarios/tier-2-3-scope-explicitly-placed.md:29:  rewrite, (2) skills/principles [optional, not mandatory], (3) organization & navigation."
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/scenarios/tier-2-3-scope-explicitly-placed.md:30:- An early Scope Contract that enumerated only tier-1 items and left tier-2/3 unlabeled.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/scenarios/tier-2-3-scope-explicitly-placed.md:31:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/scenarios/tier-2-3-scope-explicitly-placed.md:32:## Expected behavior
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/scenarios/tier-2-3-scope-explicitly-placed.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/scenarios/tier-2-3-scope-explicitly-placed.md:34:Every user-ratified scope tier is explicitly named in the Scope Contract's In-Scope block with:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/scenarios/tier-2-3-scope-explicitly-placed.md:35:- Its priority label (primary / optional / tertiary).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/scenarios/tier-2-3-scope-explicitly-placed.md:36:- Its bounded definition (what it covers, what it excludes).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/scenarios/tier-2-3-scope-explicitly-placed.md:37:- Its deferred items (what is explicitly out of scope for this tier this session).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/scenarios/tier-2-3-scope-explicitly-placed.md:38:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/scenarios/tier-2-3-scope-explicitly-placed.md:39:If a tier's content was decided to not ship this session, that must be stated directly ("not this
