.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/design/naming-convention-enforcement.md:11:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/design/naming-convention-enforcement.md:12:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/design/naming-convention-enforcement.md:13:# Naming Convention Enforcement via Consistency-Perspective Evaluator Check
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/design/naming-convention-enforcement.md:14:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/design/naming-convention-enforcement.md:15:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/design/naming-convention-enforcement.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/design/naming-convention-enforcement.md:17:Memory-file naming and staging-shape violations (bulk files instead of per-finding `{slug}.md`, wrong finding-type vocabulary, mis-routed domains) were being caught only after the fact, by the Wrap-up detection pass. By then the violating files already exist and must be cleaned up. The design needs an earlier signal that catches staging-shape-and-naming problems at evaluation time, before promotion.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/design/naming-convention-enforcement.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/design/naming-convention-enforcement.md:19:## Approach
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/design/naming-convention-enforcement.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/design/naming-convention-enforcement.md:21:Add one row to the Coverage Ownership Matrix in `evaluation/SKILL.md`, mapping the cross-cutting concern "Memorization staging shape + naming" to the Consistency + Aesthetics perspectives, and add a cross-link from `memorization/SKILL.md § Path Conventions` pointing at the new matrix row. The row content (the full wording the user selected at the Planning DISCUSSION) is:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/design/naming-convention-enforcement.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/design/naming-convention-enforcement.md:23:| Cross-cutting concern | Owning perspective(s) | What's verified |
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/design/naming-convention-enforcement.md:24:|---|---|---|
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/design/naming-convention-enforcement.md:25:| **Memorization staging shape + naming** | Consistency + Aesthetics | Per-finding `{slug}.md` filename convention (no bulk files); 5-Type vocabulary (`scenario_gap` / `checklist_gap` / `design_flaw` / `assumption_risk` / `general`) in frontmatter; Domain routing matches `evaluation/SKILL.md § Complete Domain → staging destination routing`; Slug+collision policy compliance per `evaluation/SKILL.md` § Slug + collision policy |
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/design/naming-convention-enforcement.md:26:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/design/naming-convention-enforcement.md:27:## Rationale
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/design/naming-convention-enforcement.md:28:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/design/naming-convention-enforcement.md:29:The Wrap-up detection pass is a back-stop that fires after violations exist. The Coverage Ownership Matrix row moves the same check to every loop's EVALUATION gate, where the Consistency + Aesthetics perspectives already run — so the violation is caught before the file is promoted, at zero new infrastructure cost (no new gate, no new pass; just one more row the existing perspectives consult).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/design/naming-convention-enforcement.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/design/naming-convention-enforcement.md:31:## Alternatives considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/design/naming-convention-enforcement.md:32:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/design/naming-convention-enforcement.md:33:- **A bash one-liner in `wrap-up/SKILL.md` Step 2.5 checking for missing `mistake-candidate:` frontmatter** — rejected: too narrow, it only catches one frontmatter key. The matrix-row approach generalizes to all staging types and all naming/shape rules.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/design/naming-convention-enforcement.md:34:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/design/naming-convention-enforcement.md:35:## Consequences
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/design/naming-convention-enforcement.md:36:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/design/naming-convention-enforcement.md:37:`evaluation/SKILL.md` carries the new matrix row, and `memorization/SKILL.md § Path Conventions` cross-links to it. Verification: `grep -A1 "staging shape\|staging shape + naming" evaluation/SKILL.md` returns the new row, and `grep "Coverage Ownership Matrix" memorization/SKILL.md` returns at least one hit.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/evaluation/design/naming-convention-enforcement.md:38:
