.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:13:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:14:# Planning Decisions — Env-Var Audit + SessionStart Hook task decomposition
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:16:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:18:The Planning loop decomposed the env-var-audit + SessionStart-hook feature into an Execution-ready task plan. The plan went through three dual-system evaluation rounds plus a final user-authorized manager polish before it was Execution-ready. This record captures the final decision, the fixes that shaped it, and the deferred scope.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:20:## Decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:22:**The Planning loop closed at PASS-equivalent — the plan is Execution-ready.** The decomposition splits the work into executor tasks plus manager-direct steps (worktree creation, PR-merge, post-merge stamping) that respect the manager/executor boundary in `git/SKILL.md`. The plan reached its final shape after three evaluation rounds and a user-authorized closing polish.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:24:## Rationale
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:25:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:26:The plan was refined across three evaluation rounds:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:28:**First round — REVISE.** Claude returned PASS-with-5-Medium (worktree creation underdocumented as a discrete task); Codex returned REVISE on 5 High findings, all centered on the final verification task crossing the manager/executor boundary by doing `git push` + `gh pr create` (a violation of `git/SKILL.md` Memory Access Matrix + Forbidden Operations + Procedures P4/P5). User triage accepted 6 fixes (FIX I–VI):
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:30:- **FIX I** — Added a manager-direct pre-execution step for worktree creation (git Procedure P2).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:31:- **FIX II** — Split the final verification task into executor-only verification (no push/PR/merge) and created a manager-direct PR-merge step (git Procedures P4 + P5 + P7: push, PR-open, CI watch, squash-merge, post-merge sync, worktree cleanup).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:32:- **FIX III** — Moved the manager session.json stamp step to AFTER squash-merge; it stamps on main-tree develop, not in the worktree.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:33:- **FIX IV** — Added the canonical `AI-Provenance-Record:` trailer to all commit-message blocks (`git/conventions.md` § Commit Trailers); no `Co-Authored-By:`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:34:- **FIX V** — Fully inlined the final verification block; replaced `<worktree-path>` placeholders with a `${WORKTREE_PATH}` env var; added concrete runnable commands (the transcript-path reword check, the FIX C shell-safety fixture, and the `orchestration/SKILL.md` transcriptPath grep).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:35:- **FIX VI** — Added a `gh auth status` re-verify to the PR-merge preconditions (per the Preparation `gh auth` dispute disposition).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:36:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:37:**Second round — REVISE.** Both Claude and Codex caught remaining grammar/template issues: commit subject lengths >72, the merge PR title >72, unresolved `<main-tree root>` placeholders, a PR-body placeholder, and a missing pre-remove gate. User triage accepted 5 fixes (FIX α–ε):
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:38:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:39:- **FIX α** — Three commit subjects shortened to fit ≤72 chars.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:40:- **FIX β** — Merge PR title shortened (99→64 chars).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:41:- **FIX γ** — 5 `<main-tree root>` placeholders replaced with the concrete path `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:42:- **FIX δ** — Merge PR body rewritten per the `conventions.md` PR template (4 sections + AI-Provenance-Record note).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:43:- **FIX ε** — Added an explicit pre-remove gate to the cleanup step (`git status --short` empty + `git branch --contains HEAD develop`, per `git/SKILL.md` Procedure P5 step 3); no `--force`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:44:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:45:**Third round (final).** Claude returned PASS-with-Low (a PR-body section-order deviation); Codex returned REVISE (a `--body "<placeholder>"` left in a bash command line).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:46:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:47:**Closing manager polish (user-authorized).** Given the dual-system divergence at the final round, the user authorized a manager-direct surgical fix to close the loop: the PR body was inlined via a HEREDOC (making the bash command literally executable), and the PR-body sections were reordered to the canonical `conventions.md` order (Summary → Changes → Test plan → Linked issues). The effective Planning verdict is PASS-equivalent.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:48:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:49:## Alternatives considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:50:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:51:The following were explicitly deferred out of the plan's scope (per the Plan's Deferred Items):
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:52:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:53:- Plugin mirror sync — excluded by the user's setup answer.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:54:- Runtime CLI code under `packages/cli/src/` — excluded by the user's setup answer.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:55:- TS+bun port of the hook — deferred to a future session per the user's setup answer.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:56:- The jq @sh env-passthrough quoting example — staged in the Ideation backlog.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:57:- The subagent CCSI-semantics finding — staged in the Ideation backlog.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:58:- CLI automation of `session.json` transcriptPath stamping — deferred per the stamping-mechanism disambiguation (FIX A in `env-file-load-semantics-decisions.md`).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:59:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:60:## Consequences
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:61:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:62:- The plan is Execution-ready with no open Planning questions; the manager dispatches the worktree-creation step first on advance to Execution.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:63:- All user-facing Planning decisions classified (per `discussion/SKILL.md` Decision Classification) as: 3 × `ask: design` (plan-level structure, merge PR body template, worktree-creation framing); 4 × `ask: scope` (the REVISE-vs-accept call on each round plus the closing manager-polish authorization); 0 × `user-challenge`; 0 × `auto-decide`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:64:- The manager/executor boundary is baked into the plan: executors verify only; the manager performs push, PR-open, merge, stamping, and cleanup.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:65:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/decisions/task-decomposition-decisions.md:66:## Related
