.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:15:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:17:# Context budget + wave-ordering hazard — Planning must inherit it
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:19:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:21:The Ideation framing explicitly flagged that the population to retrofit is large (208 files / 191 content docs) and that Planning should split waves into bounded tasks against the `manager-context-overflow-with-large-bundle` mistake.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:23:The Preparation readiness work listed that mistake as "loadable" but did NOT record it as an explicit readiness signal Planning must honor. A Performance-perspective evaluation flagged two related hazards not captured in the readiness signals:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:24:1. **Context budget bounding per wave** — the 208-file population is large; each wave needs an explicit context budget ceiling.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:25:2. **Conformance-vs-prose wave ordering hazard on shared files** — the conformance wave and the prose wave both touch the same 191 content docs. If not sequenced carefully, a conformance wave could destructively interfere with the prose wave or vice versa (e.g., prose edits that add staging-strip keys overwritten by a conformance pass that strips them again).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:26:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:27:Both are primarily Planning concerns (hence Low severity at Preparation), but the Preparation artifact is the Planning leader's starting point — leaving these implicit risks Planning producing an under-bounded wave plan.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:28:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:29:## Decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:31:TAGGED as a **Planning carry-forward readiness signal**. Planning MUST inherit these two constraints explicitly:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:32:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:33:1. **Bound each wave to a context budget** — define a maximum file-count or byte-ceiling per wave before generating the wave's task list. Reference `manager-context-overflow-with-large-bundle` mistake at task-assignment time.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:34:2. **Sequence waves so shared files are not double-touched destructively** — identify the shared-file set (191 content docs) and ensure the conformance wave and prose wave are ordered so the first wave's changes are stable before the second wave reads the same file. Do not interleave conformance + prose edits on the same file in a single wave.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:35:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:36:## Rationale
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:37:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:38:The 208-file population and multi-wave retrofit create real over-context risk. The `manager-context-overflow-with-large-bundle` mistake is a project-level trap that has caused failures before. Surfacing it at Preparation → Planning boundary is cheap; discovering it mid-wave is expensive (the wave must be split after partial edits, creating a harder-to-verify state).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:39:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:40:## Alternatives considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:41:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:42:None material — this is a constraint inherited from the Ideation output, not a new design choice.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:43:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:44:## Consequences
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:45:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:46:Planning MUST produce a wave plan that:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:47:- States a context-budget ceiling per wave (e.g., "wave processes at most N files or M bytes of file content per executor delegation").
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:48:- Explicitly sequences the conformance and prose waves so the same content file is not touched by both in an interleaved or reverse order.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:49:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:50:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:51:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:52:- [`manager-context-overflow-with-large-bundle`](../../../mistakes/manager-context-overflow-with-large-bundle.md) — the project mistake that motivates the per-wave budget ceiling
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:53:- [`prose-tasks-exceed-context-ceiling`](prose-tasks-exceed-context-ceiling.md) — the Planning-side decision that applied this ceiling by splitting over-large prose tasks
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:54:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/context-budget-wave-ordering-carry-forward.md:55:## Source
