.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/markdown-memory-atomicity.md:18:# Markdown-wiki agent memory + Zettelkasten atomicity (Karpathy / A-Mem)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/markdown-memory-atomicity.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/markdown-memory-atomicity.md:20:## Insight
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/markdown-memory-atomicity.md:21:Human-readable atomic markdown pages — one record, one concept — plus an index/navigation layer outperform vector-DB RAG for agent memory retrieval. The Zettelkasten atomicity principle and an explicit index are the load-bearing structure, not the embedding store.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/markdown-memory-atomicity.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/markdown-memory-atomicity.md:23:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/markdown-memory-atomicity.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/markdown-memory-atomicity.md:25:- [frontmatter-as-schema](frontmatter-as-schema.md) — the schema layer that makes the atomic pages filterable
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/markdown-memory-atomicity.md:26:- [`memorization/rules.md` §3](../../../skills/memorization/rules.md) — the gobbi one-record-one-concept atomicity rule this validates
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/markdown-memory-atomicity.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/markdown-memory-atomicity.md:28:## Why it applies
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/markdown-memory-atomicity.md:29:Confirms gobbi's "plain markdown trees, one record one concept, README index" architecture is the right shape for agent memory — so this session's job is to *raise quality within that shape*, not re-architect it. Atomicity is already gobbi rule §3 and is validated; the missing piece is per-page writing quality + an index/navigation layer (the tertiary, mostly-deferred scope). Invoke to justify NOT re-homing #272's structure and to scope the navigation layer if ever picked up.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/markdown-memory-atomicity.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/markdown-memory-atomicity.md:31:## Source
