.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/adr-decision-record-shape.md:26:- [`decisions/` template](../../../skills/memorization/templates/decisions.md) — the gobbi decision-doc template this ADR shape anchors
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/adr-decision-record-shape.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/adr-decision-record-shape.md:28:## Why it applies
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/adr-decision-record-shape.md:29:gobbi's `decisions/` + `design/` docs already approximate this (Context / Decision / Rationale / Consequences / Validation). ADR validates keeping that section contract as the per-type required sections for decisions+design, and names the section gobbi docs under-use: a Consequences / Trade-offs section that records the downsides. Invoke when defining the per-type section contract (D4) and when retrofitting decision/design bodies in the prose wave.
