.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/references/claude-code-transcript-tooluseresult-empirical.md:80:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/references/claude-code-transcript-tooluseresult-empirical.md:81:## Why it applies
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/references/claude-code-transcript-tooluseresult-empirical.md:82:The PostToolUse hook and shell-script reconstructor both consume from the same authoritative source (transcript JSONL `toolUseResult`). The hook reads the transcript at fire time (using `$CLAUDE_TRANSCRIPT_PATH` from its stdin), the reconstructor reads at session-end time. The schema gaps surfaced above (`step`, `phase`, `iter`, `model`) inform the design of the delegation prompt structure (these fields must be parseable from the prompt body — e.g., the leader prompt's first three lines already include "Your phase: ideation", "Your iteration: 1", "Your sub-step: C"). This reference demonstrates empirically that per-spawn metadata IS observable from the transcript.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/references/claude-code-transcript-tooluseresult-empirical.md:83:
