.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/diataxis-type-purity.md:18:# Diátaxis type-purity — one doc, one type's job
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/diataxis-type-purity.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/diataxis-type-purity.md:20:## Insight
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/diataxis-type-purity.md:21:A doc serves one of four jobs along two axes (action vs cognition, study vs work); "crossing or blurring the boundaries … is at the heart of a vast number of problems." The positive rule is: each doc does exactly one type's job and must not bleed into another.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/diataxis-type-purity.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/diataxis-type-purity.md:23:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/diataxis-type-purity.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/diataxis-type-purity.md:25:- [`naming-standard-needs-positive-guidance-not-just-blocklist`](../../../mistakes/naming-standard-needs-positive-guidance-not-just-blocklist.md) — the project mistake whose "name the positive bar, not just a blocklist" lesson this reference reinforces for prose
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/diataxis-type-purity.md:26:- [adr-decision-record-shape](adr-decision-record-shape.md) — the companion reference anchoring the per-type section contract
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/diataxis-type-purity.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/diataxis-type-purity.md:28:## Why it applies
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/diataxis-type-purity.md:29:gobbi already HAS a type system (decisions / design / mistakes / learnings / notes / references), but the existing standard governs naming/frontmatter/structure, not prose-content type-purity. Diátaxis supplies the positive prose rule the standard lacks — a decision is not a journal; a design doc is not a changelog. It maps onto Principle 13's existing "must NOT bleed into adjacent types" clause, extending it from a frontmatter-type rule to a prose-content rule. Invoke when writing or evaluating any memory doc for single-type focus.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/diataxis-type-purity.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/references/diataxis-type-purity.md:31:## Source
