.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:1:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:2:name: archive-glob-scope-leak
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:3:description: "Design flaw: plan's bare ** globs for files: patterns match archive/ subdirs that are explicitly out of scope; fix by adding archive-exclusion predicates."
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:4:tags: [archive, glob, scope, conformance]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:5:created: 2026-05-26
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:6:session: b0a0eaf9-03f7-4dce-a040-c7443653a459
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:7:type: decisions
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:8:domain: docs-sync
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:9:status: accepted
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:10:scope: feature
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:11:feature: project-memory
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:12:supersedes: null
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:13:superseded_by: null
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:14:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:16:# Archive glob scope leak in plan's `**` `files:` globs
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:18:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:20:An early version of the retrofit plan used bare `**` `files:` globs (e.g., `features/workflow/**/*.md`) for several conformance and prose tasks. The project-memory tree includes frozen `archive/` subdirs that the scope contract's Out-of-Scope section explicitly excludes from every wave. The naive `**` glob would have matched those frozen docs.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:22:## Decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:24:Confirmed as a design flaw. Every `**` glob must carry `exclude: "**/archive/**"` in `files:` AND `-not -path '*/archive/*'` in the `verifies` gate, so the edit-glob matches the count predicate exactly.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:25:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:26:## Rationale
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:28:The 7 frozen docs (2 content + 5 READMEs) are enumerated in the plan's counts note. The `verifies` git-diff check does not detect archive edits — the edit-glob exclusion is the structural fix. Three independent evaluation perspectives (Project, Consistency, Risk) converged on this root.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:30:## Alternatives considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:31:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:32:Explicit `not-path` in `verifies` only (no glob exclusion) — rejected: the edit-glob would still touch the frozen docs even if the verify caught it post-hoc.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:34:## Consequences
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:35:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:36:All `**` globs in the plan now carry `exclude: "**/archive/**"`. The tasks that enumerate typed subdirs explicitly are archive-clean by construction. The conformance-wave counts now match the count predicate (workflow 26, install-runtime 44, READMEs 18).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:37:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:38:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:39:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:40:- [`memorization/rules.md` §4.6](../../../skills/memorization/rules.md) — the standard's archive-exclusion scope edge this glob fix enforces
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:41:- [`plans/2026-05-26-dev-doc-standard-retrofit`](../plans/2026-05-26-dev-doc-standard-retrofit.md) — the plan whose globs were made archive-safe
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:42:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:43:## Source
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:44:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/project-memory/decisions/archive-glob-scope-leak.md:45:Originating session `b0a0eaf9-03f7-4dce-a040-c7443653a459` (see the `session` frontmatter field) — Planning review, Project / Consistency / Risk perspectives + Codex F1.
