.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/discussions/scope-contract-lock.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/discussions/scope-contract-lock.md:16:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/discussions/scope-contract-lock.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/discussions/scope-contract-lock.md:18:Before the PostToolUse hook task could be planned, it had to be settled whether the existing `session.template.json.agents[]` schema needed changes — a template bump would have added a schema-edit task to Planning and Execution.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/discussions/scope-contract-lock.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/discussions/scope-contract-lock.md:20:## Question
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/discussions/scope-contract-lock.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/discussions/scope-contract-lock.md:22:Does the existing `session.template.json.agents[]` schema have gaps that need to be filled before the PostToolUse hook task ships?
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/discussions/scope-contract-lock.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/discussions/scope-contract-lock.md:24:## Options considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/discussions/scope-contract-lock.md:25:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/discussions/scope-contract-lock.md:26:- Treat the existing template schema as sufficient and write the new `status` field as an extra-property, deferring a formal template bump (the recommended option).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/discussions/scope-contract-lock.md:27:- Bump the template schema this session to add the `status` field formally, adding a schema-edit task to Planning/Execution.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/discussions/scope-contract-lock.md:28:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/discussions/scope-contract-lock.md:29:## User decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/discussions/scope-contract-lock.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/discussions/scope-contract-lock.md:31:Confirmed the recommended option: the template schema is sufficient; no template change this session. The `status` field is an extra-property write (not in the template); a formal template bump is deferred to the `schema-extension-agents-status-field` backlog item.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/discussions/scope-contract-lock.md:32:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/discussions/scope-contract-lock.md:33:## Implication
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/discussions/scope-contract-lock.md:34:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/discussions/scope-contract-lock.md:35:The PostToolUse hook task ships without modifying `session.template.json`. The hook writes `status` as an extra-property on failed spawn entries; Planning and Execution do not need to include a template-edit task.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/discussions/scope-contract-lock.md:36:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/discussions/scope-contract-lock.md:37:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/discussions/scope-contract-lock.md:38:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/discussions/scope-contract-lock.md:39:- Backlog [`../backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md`](../backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md) — the deferred formal template bump.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/discussions/scope-contract-lock.md:40:- `discussions/dual-hook-registration-confirm.md` — the companion decision that also deferred the `status` field template extension.
