.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:1:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:2:name: rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:3:description: Planning Task 03 incorrectly described the git checkout rollback path; corrected to git rm per the Ideation rollback contract.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:4:type: decisions
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:5:scope: feature
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:6:feature: git-workflow
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:7:status: accepted
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:8:created: 2026-05-24
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:9:session: 1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:10:tags: [git-workflow, rollback, planning-correction]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:11:domain: docs-sync
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:12:supersedes: null
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:13:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:14:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:15:# Rollback semantics correction: git rm (not git checkout) after failed promote-now commit
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:17:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:19:The Planning brief for Task 03 (Preparation promote-now commit-on-branch) initially described the rollback sequence for a failed `git commit` post-copy as "restoration via git checkout, no auto-rm of skill body." This was wrong: the copied skill file did not pre-exist in the worktree, so `git checkout` has nothing to restore. The correct action is `git rm` to remove the copied file.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:21:The Ideation rollback contract (Design Decision D-3, "Partial-failure rollback") explicitly requires: if `git commit` fails post-copy, the manager MUST `git -C "$worktreePath" rm <copied-paths>` to remove the copied skill body before surfacing the failure to the user via AskUserQuestion.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:23:## Decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:25:The Planning brief was corrected during Planning review to align with the Ideation rollback contract. The rollback sequence is now:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:26:1. `git commit` fails post-copy
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:27:2. Manager runs `git -C "$worktreePath" rm <copied-paths>` — REMOVES the copied file (not `git checkout`)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:28:3. AskUserQuestion surfaces the failure to the user
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:29:4. Re-attempt or abort per user response
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:31:## Rationale
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:32:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:33:The copied file did not pre-exist in the worktree before the promote-now operation. A `git checkout` would either fail (no prior version) or restore to HEAD (which also has no version of this file). The only correct recovery is removal.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:34:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:35:## Alternatives considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:36:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:37:- **`git checkout <copied-paths>` (the original, incorrect brief wording)** — rejected: there is no prior version of the copied file to restore. `git checkout` either errors out (no tracked version) or restores to HEAD, which also has no version of the file, leaving the stray copy in place. It cannot undo the copy.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:38:- **Leave the copied file in place and surface the commit failure** — rejected: a half-promoted skill body left in the worktree is the partial-promotion failure the rollback contract exists to prevent; the worktree would carry an uncommitted, orphaned file.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:39:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:40:## Consequences
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:41:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:42:The verification spec for the Preparation promote-now implementation now includes grep gates confirming `git -C "$worktreePath" rm` and AskUserQuestion co-location in the shipped Preparation promote-now text. Any executor implementing the promote-now rollback path must use `git rm` to remove the copied file, not `git checkout`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:43:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:44:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:45:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:46:- `design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md` — the commit-on-branch design (D-3) whose partial-failure rollback this decision corrects.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:47:- `discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md` — the discussion that placed this rollback's documentation home in `preparation/SKILL.md`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:48:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:49:## Source
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:50:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md:51:Full session context at `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-24-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/planning/`
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:1:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:2:name: five-locked-decisions
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:3:description: Five user-confirmed locked decisions for session-foundations-bundle-b Execution — non-negotiable during task execution.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:4:type: design
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:5:scope: feature
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:6:feature: workflow
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:7:status: accepted
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:8:created: 2026-05-24
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:9:session: 1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:10:tags: [planning, locked-decisions, execution, wave-ordering]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:11:title: 5 locked decisions for session-foundations-bundle-b execution
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:12:related:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:13:  - planning/artifacts/plan.md
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:14:  - ideation/artifacts/bundle-b-ideation-pass.md
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:15:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:17:# 5 locked decisions for Execution
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:19:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:21:Before the session-foundations-bundle-b Execution loop began, five design choices needed to be settled and held fixed so executors would not re-open them mid-implementation: the wave ordering, the hook/reconstructor delegation shape, which mistakes each task brief cites, and where two pieces of documentation live (rollback semantics and the direct-mode opt-out). Each was surfaced to the user via AskUserQuestion during the Planning DISCUSSION phase.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:23:## Decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:25:Lock the five choices below. All five were user-confirmed; they are non-negotiable during Execution — executors must not re-litigate them.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:26:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:27:### Strict wave ordering: T1 completes before T3 (LOCK #1)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:28:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:29:**Decision**: T1 wave (Tasks 01-06) completes before T3 wave (Tasks 07-10). No interleaving.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:31:**Rationale**: coherent commit history per the per-iter cadence rule; T1 doc edits land as one wave commit before the T3 wave starts. Avoids interleaving ambiguity on `orchestration/SKILL.md` (touched by both waves).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:32:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:33:**Mechanism**: dependency edges `05 → 07` AND `06 → 07` graph-enforce the gate. Both terminal T1 leaves must complete.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:34:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:35:### Shared-executor delegation for hook and reconstructor (LOCK #2)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:36:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:37:**Decision**: One executor delegation covers both Task 07 (hook script) and Task 08 (reconstructor) back-to-back.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:38:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:39:**Rationale**: Task 08 consumes jq snippets and the hook stdin contract established by Task 07. A shared execution context avoids requiring Task 08 to re-derive that contract.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:40:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:41:**Mechanism**: Manager issues one delegation prompt covering both tasks; executor completes Task 07 first, then Task 08, within the same context window.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:42:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:43:### Mistake-bundle scope: Iron Law 7 only for T3 tasks (LOCK #3)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:44:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:45:**Decision**: T3 task briefs (Tasks 07-10) cite only `manager-iter2-brief-failed-iron-law-7-verbatim-spec-recheck.md`. The other two T1 mistakes (cwd routing, rm -rf safety) are NOT extended to T3.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:46:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:47:**Rationale**: T3 tasks do not write to session paths (cwd-routing mistake is inapplicable) and do not remove files (rm -rf safety is inapplicable). T3 tasks DO involve verbatim citation of hook stdin contract, structured-header regexes, and JSON schema field names — exactly the Iron Law 7 failure mode.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:48:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:49:### Rollback semantics home: preparation/SKILL.md (LOCK #4)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:50:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:51:**Decision**: Rollback semantics for the `generate-now` promote-now path live co-located with the narrow-exception text in `preparation/SKILL.md`. NOT in `git/SKILL.md`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:52:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:53:**Rationale**: single-source-of-truth — the rollback applies to the promote-now procedure in preparation/SKILL.md; co-locating preserves readability. `git/SKILL.md` retains the general critical-rule paragraph only.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:54:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:55:**Rollback sequence**: on `git commit` failure post-copy: `git -C "$worktreePath" rm <copied-paths>` → AskUserQuestion → re-attempt or abort. This REMOVES the copied file (not `git checkout`, since the file did not pre-exist).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:56:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:57:### Direct-mode opt-out home: orchestration/SKILL.md row 5.5 footnote (LOCK #5)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:58:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:59:**Decision**: Direct-mode opt-out ("if `workflow.git.mode = 'direct'`, row 5.5 is skipped and `worktreePath` remains null") is documented as a row 5.5 footnote in `orchestration/SKILL.md`. NOT in `git/SKILL.md`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:60:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:61:**Rationale**: co-locates the opt-out flag with the row it opts out of; avoids a third cross-skill reference.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:62:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:63:## Rationale
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:64:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:65:Each lock removes a degree of freedom that, left open, would let an executor make an incompatible choice mid-flight: the wave order keeps the commit history coherent and avoids interleaving ambiguity on shared files; the shared-executor delegation preserves the jq/stdin context Task 08 needs from Task 07; the narrowed mistake-bundle cites only the Iron Law 7 mistake on T3 because the cwd-routing and rm-rf mistakes are inapplicable to script-authoring tasks; and the two documentation-home choices co-locate each rule with the procedure it governs to keep a single source of truth.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:66:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:67:## Alternatives considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:68:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:69:- **Interleaved waves / advisory ordering (vs LOCK #1).** Rejected: interleaving the doc-edit and script waves blurs commit history and creates ordering ambiguity on `orchestration/SKILL.md`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:70:- **Separate executors for hook and reconstructor (vs LOCK #2).** Rejected: the second executor would have to re-derive the jq snippets and stdin contract.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:71:- **Extending all three T1 mistakes to T3 briefs (vs LOCK #3).** Rejected: the cwd-routing and rm-rf mistakes do not apply to T3 tasks; only the Iron Law 7 verbatim-citation mistake does.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:72:- **Documenting rollback and the direct-mode opt-out in `git/SKILL.md` (vs LOCK #4/#5).** Rejected: that splits each rule from the procedure it governs and adds cross-skill references.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:73:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:74:## Consequences
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:75:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:76:Execution proceeds with these five choices fixed. The wave gate is graph-enforced (`05 → 07`, `06 → 07`); the manager issues one delegation for Tasks 07-08; T3 briefs cite only the Iron Law 7 mistake; rollback semantics live in `preparation/SKILL.md` and the direct-mode opt-out lives as a row-5.5 footnote in `orchestration/SKILL.md`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:77:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:78:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:79:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:80:- `design/dependency-graph-strict-wave-ordering.md` — the graph that enforces LOCK #1.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:81:- `decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md` — the decision record for the LOCK #1 edges.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/five-locked-decisions.md:82:- `backlogs/lock2-shared-executor-mega-task-risk.md` — the deferred context-budget risk from LOCK #2.
