.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/langgraph-skill-catalog-pattern.md:16:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/langgraph-skill-catalog-pattern.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/langgraph-skill-catalog-pattern.md:18:# LangGraph deep-agents skill catalog pattern
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/langgraph-skill-catalog-pattern.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/langgraph-skill-catalog-pattern.md:20:## Insight
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/langgraph-skill-catalog-pattern.md:21:LangGraph's deep-agents framework formalizes "skills" as a first-class concept: domain knowledge lives outside the prompt and is loaded only when a task requires it. The system prompt includes a structured **list of available skills containing name, description, tags, and supporting file names** — small enough to include in every request — and the agent pulls in detailed instructions only when needed. This is the pattern the planned skill-loading matrix is reaching for in reverse: gobbi already has per-skill SKILL.md files at the leaves; what is missing is the structured catalog at the top that names exactly which skills each (role, phase) needs.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/langgraph-skill-catalog-pattern.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/langgraph-skill-catalog-pattern.md:23:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/langgraph-skill-catalog-pattern.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/langgraph-skill-catalog-pattern.md:25:- `rbac-matrix-single-source-of-truth` — the companion external-prior-art reference for the same role × phase skill-matrix design (centralized authoritative matrix that all consumers read from).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/langgraph-skill-catalog-pattern.md:26:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/langgraph-skill-catalog-pattern.md:27:## Why it applies
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/langgraph-skill-catalog-pattern.md:28:The planned role × phase skill matrix needs a shape. The LangGraph skill-catalog pattern provides one validated answer — a structured catalog (matrix) listing each skill with name + description + tags + file names. Adapted to gobbi: a role × phase table where each cell lists the canonical skill files. The deeper architectural takeaway is that the framework treats this catalog as *part of the system prompt* — i.e., it is something every agent sees on every request. In gobbi terms, this maps to the Load Directives block — the catalog *is* the Load Directives content. The matrix and the Load Directives block are two views of the same data; the validator's job is to keep them in sync.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/langgraph-skill-catalog-pattern.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/langgraph-skill-catalog-pattern.md:30:## Source
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/langgraph-skill-catalog-pattern.md:31:- https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/deepagents/skills
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/langgraph-skill-catalog-pattern.md:32:- https://pessini.medium.com/stop-stuffing-your-system-prompt-build-scalable-agent-skills-in-langgraph-a9856378e8f6
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/langgraph-skill-catalog-pattern.md:33:- Both accessed 2026-05-23
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/langgraph-skill-catalog-pattern.md:34:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/langgraph-skill-catalog-pattern.md:35:## Excerpt
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/langgraph-skill-catalog-pattern.md:36:> "LangGraph supports a skills system where domain knowledge lives outside the prompt and is loaded only when a task requires it, allowing agents to see a lightweight catalog first and pull in detailed instructions only when needed."
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/langgraph-skill-catalog-pattern.md:37:
