.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:8:created: 2026-05-23
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:9:session: 1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:10:tags: [hooks, transcript, correlation, tool-use-id]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:11:design-id: D-3-6
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:12:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:13:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:14:# Transcript correlation key: tool_use_id
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:16:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:18:Both the hook and the reconstructor must match a Task spawn (its input-side `tool_use` line) to the subagent's result (its `toolUseResult` line) in the transcript JSONL. An early evaluation finding flagged that the design said "read the transcript line by `tool_use_id`" without specifying the exact jq path. A single, always-available correlation key was needed.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:20:## Decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:22:The hook uses `tool_use_id` from its stdin to locate the matching transcript lines. Two jq lookup paths:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:24:1. **Locate the tool_use line** (input side):
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:25:   ```
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:26:   jq -r '.message.content[]? | select(.type == "tool_use" and .id == $tool_use_id)'
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:27:   ```
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:28:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:29:2. **Locate the toolUseResult line** (result side):
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:30:   ```
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:31:   jq -r '. | select(.toolUseResult != null) | select(.message.content[]?.tool_use_id == $tool_use_id)'
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:32:   ```
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:34:**Reconstructor** walks the JSONL in order; for each `tool_use` line where `tool_input.subagent_type` is non-null (Task spawn), finds the corresponding `toolUseResult` line later in the file by `tool_use_id` match.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:35:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:36:## Rationale
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:37:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:38:A first-iteration Codex finding flagged that the design said "read transcript line by `tool_use_id`" without the exact jq path. The hook always has `tool_use_id` in its stdin; the reconstructor has both keys (`tool_use_id` and `toolUseResult.agentId`) available from the transcript. Using `tool_use_id` is the always-available, hook-consistent key.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:39:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:40:Supporting evidence anchored at decision time: the first-iteration Codex finding (the missing exact jq path); the transcript `toolUseResult` empirical reference under `references/`; and empirical stdin and transcript inspection confirming `tool_use_id` availability.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:41:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:42:## Alternatives considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:43:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:44:- Correlate by `toolUseResult.agentId` only — rejected: hook stdin does not contain `agentId` directly; `tool_use_id` is always available.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:45:- Time-based correlation (newest line) — rejected: race-prone if transcript flush lags.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:46:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:47:## Consequences
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:48:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:49:- Both the hook (stdin correlation) and the reconstructor (transcript walk) use `tool_use_id` as the join key, with the two jq lookup paths above.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:50:- Validation obligation: a single-script verifier on a fixture transcript asserting the jq path returns exactly one line for a known `tool_use_id` and zero lines for an unknown id.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:51:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:52:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/tool-use-id-correlation-key.md:53:
