.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:8:created: 2026-05-24
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:9:session: 1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:10:tags: [planning, wave-ordering, lock1, dependency-graph]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:11:topic: T1→T3 wave ordering — strict sequential or interleaved?
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:12:outcome: Strict sequential confirmed; graph-enforced via LOCK #1 (05,06 → 07)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:13:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:14:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:15:# Wave ordering: strict sequential T1→T3 (workflow waves)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:17:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:19:The plan proposes running T1 tasks (01-06) before T3 tasks (07-10). The leader asked the user to confirm whether this should be strictly sequential or merely recommended (allowing interleaving if an executor wanted to run Task 06 after Task 07, for example).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:21:## Question
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:23:Should the T1 wave complete before the T3 wave starts (strict ordering), or is the ordering advisory (executors can interleave if it seems safe)?
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:25:## Options considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:26:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:27:1. **Strict sequential** — graph-enforced: LOCK #1 is the canonical choice. Tasks 07-10 cannot start until all of Tasks 01-06 complete. Rationale: coherent commit history, one wave per commit, avoids interleaving ambiguity on shared files.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:28:2. **Advisory ordering** — prose-only: leader recommends the sequence but the dependency graph doesn't enforce it. Executors can interleave at their discretion.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:30:## User decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:31:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:32:Strict sequential confirmed. LOCK #1 applies as strict ordering, not advisory.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:34:## Implication
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:35:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:36:The dependency graph uses edges `05 → 07` AND `06 → 07` (both terminal T1 leaves gate Task 07). Neither 05 nor 06 alone gates 07 — both do. The graph was strengthened to this form from an earlier draft that gated Task 07 on `requires: [05]` only.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:37:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:38:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:39:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:40:- `decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md` — the decision record that added the gating edges.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-wave-ordering-sequential-t1-t3.md:41:- `design/dependency-graph-strict-wave-ordering.md` — the design capturing the full wave-ordering graph.
