.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/skill-loading-discipline-root-cause.md:12:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/skill-loading-discipline-root-cause.md:13:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/skill-loading-discipline-root-cause.md:14:# Root-cause hypothesis for skill-loading discipline confirmed
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/skill-loading-discipline-root-cause.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/skill-loading-discipline-root-cause.md:16:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/skill-loading-discipline-root-cause.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/skill-loading-discipline-root-cause.md:18:While framing the skill-loading-discipline improvement (the T2 topic), the leader proposed a composite root cause: agents fail to load instructed skills both because of a documentation gap (D) and because of lazy-load behavior (L). The leader asked the user to confirm this (D+L) composite before any design built on it.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/skill-loading-discipline-root-cause.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/skill-loading-discipline-root-cause.md:20:## Question
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/skill-loading-discipline-root-cause.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/skill-loading-discipline-root-cause.md:22:Is the root cause for the skill-loading-discipline topic a (D+L) composite — a documentation gap plus lazy-load behavior?
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/skill-loading-discipline-root-cause.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/skill-loading-discipline-root-cause.md:24:## Options considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/skill-loading-discipline-root-cause.md:25:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/skill-loading-discipline-root-cause.md:26:1. **(D+L) composite (Recommended)** — both a docs gap and lazy-load behavior drive the failures.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/skill-loading-discipline-root-cause.md:27:2. **Single-cause** — either docs-only or behavior-only.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/skill-loading-discipline-root-cause.md:28:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/skill-loading-discipline-root-cause.md:29:## User decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/skill-loading-discipline-root-cause.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/skill-loading-discipline-root-cause.md:31:Confirmed the (D+L) composite: 3 of 7 promoted mistakes fit the pattern of agents failing to load skills they were instructed to load.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/skill-loading-discipline-root-cause.md:32:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/skill-loading-discipline-root-cause.md:33:## Implication
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/skill-loading-discipline-root-cause.md:34:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/skill-loading-discipline-root-cause.md:35:The (D+L) composite analysis is preserved in the skill-loading-discipline backlog for when the T2 topic is picked up in a future session. It does not affect the T1 or T3 design in the current session's scope.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/skill-loading-discipline-root-cause.md:36:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/skill-loading-discipline-root-cause.md:37:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/skill-loading-discipline-root-cause.md:38:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/discussions/skill-loading-discipline-root-cause.md:39:- `../../../backlogs/skill-loading-discipline.md` — the deferred T2 backlog item carrying this root-cause analysis.
