.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:1:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:2:name: drop-legacy-setup-questions
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:3:description: Replace the 2-question setup block in gobbi/SKILL.md with 1 mode question plus an optional customize gate, eliminating the legacy eval-mode and git-workflow-mode questions.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:4:type: design
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:5:scope: feature
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:6:feature: workflow
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:7:status: active
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:8:created: 2026-05-23
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:9:session: 7ea62d36-e826-4ce6-9e90-9e948007b068
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:10:tags: [gobbi-skill, session-bootstrap, setup-questions, orchestration]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:11:topic: drop-legacy-setup-questions
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:12:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:13:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:14:# Drop legacy setup questions — gobbi/SKILL.md session bootstrap rewrite
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:16:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:18:The session-bootstrap step in `gobbi/SKILL.md § Step 4` asked the user two setup questions (eval-mode and git-workflow-mode). Those same defaults are already encoded in `settings.default.json` and walked through by `orchestration/SKILL.md § Step 1`'s "use defaults vs customize" gate (rows 1-2), so the two-question block duplicated and partially overlapped that mechanism — a docs-sync drift between the bootstrap prompt and the settings source of truth.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:20:## Decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:22:Rewrite `gobbi/SKILL.md § Step 4` from "ask the user 2 setup questions" to "ask 1 setup question + an optional customize gate":
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:24:- Question 1 — mode (chat/auto), **default auto** per `orchestration/templates/settings.default.json`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:25:- Optional "customize defaults?" gate — if yes, defer to the `orchestration/SKILL.md § Step 1` row-2 walk-through.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:26:- Remove the explicit eval-mode and git-workflow-mode questions; those defaults live in `settings.json`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:28:## Rationale
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:30:`orchestration/SKILL.md § Step 1` already owns the defaults-vs-customize gate, so collapsing the bootstrap to one mode question plus a customize gate resolves the duplication without losing any capability. The settings defaults were verified empirically: `jq '.mode, .workflow.ideation.evaluate.mode, .git.pr' orchestration/templates/settings.default.json` returns `"auto"`, `"always"`, `{"open": false, "draft": false}` — confirming the defaults the bootstrap no longer needs to ask about.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:31:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:32:One referenced file does not exist: there is no `.claude/skills/orchestration/workflow/configuration.md` (`find .claude/skills/orchestration/workflow -name "configuration*"` returns empty). Wherever an earlier brief pointed at that path, substitute `orchestration/SKILL.md § Step 1`, which is the authoritative configuration walk-through.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:34:## Alternatives considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:35:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:36:- **Keep the two setup questions in `gobbi/SKILL.md`.** Rejected: they duplicate the `settings.json` defaults and the `orchestration/SKILL.md § Step 1` customize gate, creating two places that can drift out of sync.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:37:- **Remove the setup block entirely (no mode question).** Rejected: the chat/auto mode choice is the one bootstrap decision that genuinely belongs at session start; only the eval-mode and git-workflow-mode questions are redundant.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:38:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:39:## Consequences
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:40:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:41:A fresh manager's bootstrap asks at most one mode question plus an optional customize gate; the eval-mode and git-workflow-mode questions are gone. Validation: `awk '/^### 4\./,/^### 5\./' gobbi/SKILL.md` shows ≤ 2 AskUserQuestion mentions (mode + customize gate) and zero mentions of "Always evaluate" / "Skip evaluation" / "Direct commit" / "Git workflow" as bootstrap-question options.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:42:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:43:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/design/drop-legacy-setup-questions.md:44:
