.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:16:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:18:# Claude Agent SDK TaskOutput interface
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:20:## Insight
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:21:The Claude Agent SDK (`@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk`) defines a TypeScript-typed `TaskOutput` interface for what the Task tool returns. Per secondary documentation references summarizing the type definitions:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:23:```typescript
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:24:interface TaskOutput {
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:25:  result: string;              // Final text response from subagent
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:26:  usage?: {
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:27:    input_tokens: number;
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:28:    output_tokens: number;
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:29:  };
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:30:  total_cost_usd?: number;
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:31:  duration_ms?: number;
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:32:}
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:33:```
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:34:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:35:This is the **public-API documented** shape — narrower than the empirically-observed `toolUseResult` payload in the transcript (which adds `agentId`, `agentType`, `cache_read_input_tokens`, `cache_creation_input_tokens`, `toolStats`, etc.). The implication: the runtime captures more telemetry than the public API formally exposes. The transcript is the source of truth for total observability; the public API is the source of truth for forward compatibility.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:36:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:37:Subagent-context fields `agent_id` and `agent_type` are also in the hook input — populated when the hook fires inside a subagent. In TypeScript, on the base hook input. In Python, only on PreToolUse / PostToolUse / PostToolUseFailure inputs.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:38:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:39:There is also a `SubagentStop` hook event (separate from `PostToolUse` on the Task tool) which fires when a subagent completes — input includes `agent_id` + `agent_transcript_path` + `stop_hook_active`. This is a parallel mechanism the agents[] hook design could consider, though it requires SDK-level configuration (not shell-command hooks via `.claude/settings.json` `hooks.*`).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:40:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:41:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:42:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:43:- `claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema` — the PostToolUse hook input schema the agents[] hook actually consumes.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:44:- `claude-code-transcript-tooluseresult-empirical` — the empirically-observed rich `toolUseResult` payload (option (b)) that this documented TaskOutput shape (option (a)) is contrasted against.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:45:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:46:## Why it applies
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:47:The agents[] hook design needs to choose between:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:48:- (a) reading `tool_result` directly from the hook stdin (TaskOutput shape — narrow but stable),
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:49:- (b) reading the rich `toolUseResult` from the transcript file (rich but version-dependent), or
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:50:- (c) using `SubagentStop` instead of `PostToolUse` (different lifecycle event, different schema).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:51:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:52:This reference establishes (a) as the public-stable surface and (b) as the empirical-rich surface. The recommended pattern is: use (b) for richness, write the hook to be resilient to schema drift (read defensively with `jq`'s `// "fallback"` defaults), and treat (a) as the contract baseline for forward compat.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:53:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:54:## Source
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:55:- https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/hooks
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:56:- https://gist.github.com/johnlindquist/d22c70fd70660b4f6fb4d0b05d0792d2
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:57:- Both accessed 2026-05-23
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:58:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:59:## Excerpt
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:60:> "interface TaskOutput { result: string; usage?: { input_tokens: number; output_tokens: number; }; total_cost_usd?: number; duration_ms?: number; }"
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:61:> "`agent_id` and `agent_type` are populated when the hook fires inside a subagent. In TypeScript, these are on the base hook input and available to all hook types."
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/references/claude-code-agent-sdk-task-output.md:62:
