.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:15:# `.gobbi/project.json` bootstrap — dormant precondition for session-dir resolver
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:17:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:19:The hook's session-dir resolver algorithm specifies two paths: step (i) — the preferred path — reads `$cwd/.gobbi/project.json` and extracts the `name` field; step (ii) — the fallback path — enumerates `$cwd/.gobbi/projects/` and selects the single directory if exactly one exists.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:21:Empirical verification on 2026-05-23 (`ls .gobbi/project.json` from the repo root): the file **does not exist** in this repo. `ls -la .gobbi/` confirms only `projects/`, `settings.json`, and `.gitignore` are present.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:23:Today the resolver falls through to step (ii) and works correctly because exactly one project directory exists (`.gobbi/projects/gobbi/`). However, step (i) is a **dormant precondition** — it is documented as preferred but cannot be exercised until the file is created.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:25:## Why deferred
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:26:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:27:The hook is functional without step (i); step (ii) is sufficient for the current single-project repo. Bumping the resolver from "step (i) preferred" to "step (i) required" would either require creating `.gobbi/project.json` as a one-line write or tolerating step (ii) indefinitely. The originating session's scope contract covered docs + scripts + `settings.json` but did not explicitly include creating `.gobbi/project.json`. Surfacing this as a backlog item keeps the resolver design honest without expanding scope mid-session. The effort is trivial — a single ~5-line JSON file write that can be folded into any hook commit — so the only reason it is deferred is scope discipline, not difficulty.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:28:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:29:## When to pick up
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:31:- At Planning (task decomposition for the next hook-authoring session): the planner may absorb the file creation into the `settings.json` registration step, since both are bootstrap-type writes.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:32:- At Execution start: the executor may add it as a one-line setup step before authoring the hook script.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:33:- At a future session when the project gains a second project under `.gobbi/projects/` — that would break step (ii)'s "exactly one directory" guard and force step (i) to be created.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:34:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:35:## Suggested approach
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:36:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:37:Two paths, picked at Execution start or later:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:38:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:39:1. **In-Execution (recommended if the executor's plan agrees)**: add a single-file write step to the Execution plan — create `.gobbi/project.json` with content `{"name": "gobbi"}`. Cost: 1 file, ~5 lines. This activates step (i) for every future session.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:40:2. **Defer to a follow-up session**: leave the file absent; the resolver continues to use step (ii); this backlog item carries forward as the witness that the dormant precondition is intentional.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:41:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:42:## Originating session
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:43:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:44:`.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/`
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:45:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:46:## Source
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:47:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:48:- The resolver's step-(i)-preferred design decision and its dormant-precondition note, recorded in the originating session's design work.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md:49:- Verified empirically on 2026-05-23: `ls -la /playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/project.json` returns "No such file or directory".
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:1:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:2:name: reconstructor-verify-and-fix
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:3:description: Reconstructor algorithm is verify-and-fix — upsert agents[] by id from transcript, idempotent, orphan-report only (no delete); protected by flock serialization.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:4:type: design
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:5:scope: feature
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:6:feature: install-runtime
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:7:status: locked
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:8:created: 2026-05-23
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:9:session: 1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:10:tags: [reconstructor, agents, session-json, idempotent]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:11:design-id: D-3-2
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:12:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:13:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:14:# Reconstructor algorithm: verify-and-fix, idempotent upsert by id, orphan-report only
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:16:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:18:The PostToolUse hook populates `session.json.agents[]` incrementally, but a session can start with an empty or partially-populated `agents[]` (e.g., after a resume, or if a hook fired before the field was seeded). A reconstructor script is needed to rebuild `agents[]` from the authoritative transcript without destroying manager-seeded entries or user hand-edits, and it must be safe to run repeatedly.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:20:## Decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:22:`.claude/scripts/reconstruct-agents.sh` algorithm:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:23:1. Takes session-dir path as argument
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:24:2. Acquires `flock -x` on `session.json` (see `flock-serialization-on-session-json.md`) BEFORE reading
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:25:3. Walks transcript JSONL; for each Task spawn (`tool_input.subagent_type` non-null), finds the corresponding `toolUseResult` by `tool_use_id` correlation (see `tool-use-id-correlation-key.md`)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:26:4. Upserts `agents[]` by `id` with last-write-wins on non-null transcript values; first-write-wins on `startedAt` + `id`
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:27:5. Reports orphan entries (entries in `agents[]` with no transcript match) as warnings only — does NOT delete
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:28:6. Writes merged `agents[]` back atomically (temp file + mv)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:29:7. Releases lock on script exit
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:31:**Idempotent**: N runs converge to the same result.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:32:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:33:## Rationale
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:34:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:35:Verify-and-fix is robust to empty-and-rebuild + partial-population; idempotent. Orphan-report-only preserves manager seed + user hand-edits. The flock serialization design ensures the reconstructor's read-modify-write does not race against an in-flight PostToolUse hook.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:36:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:37:Supporting evidence anchored at decision time: the verify-and-fix robustness rationale; transcript inspection confirming the `toolUseResult` fields are available; and the companion flock serialization design (`flock-serialization-on-session-json.md`).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:38:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:39:## Alternatives considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:40:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:41:- Scan-and-replace — rejected: deletes the manager seed.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:42:- Append-only — rejected: cannot fix partial-field entries.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:43:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:44:## Consequences
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:45:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:46:- The reconstructor (`reconstruct-agents.sh`) takes a session-dir path, acquires the flock before reading, upserts by id, reports (never deletes) orphans, and writes back atomically.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:47:- Because it is idempotent and orphan-report-only, it can be run at any time — including repeatedly — without corrupting manager-seeded or user-edited entries.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:48:- Validation obligations: a single-script verifier on a two-state fixture (empty `agents[]` + partial `agents[]`); an idempotency double-run; and a reconstructor-during-hook-fire smoke test (shared with the flock serialization design).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:49:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:50:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:51:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:52:- `flock-serialization-on-session-json.md` — the serialization the reconstructor acquires before reading.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:53:- `tool-use-id-correlation-key.md` — the correlation key the transcript walk uses.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:54:- `dual-hook-registration-resolver.md` — the hook the reconstructor backstops.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:55:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:56:## Source
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:57:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md:58:The full design narrative is preserved in the project session journal `notes/2026-05-24-session-foundations-bundle-b.md` (the session that designed and shipped the PostToolUse hook architecture).
