.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/README.md:19:The multi-agent roster — PI, planner, executors, evaluators, scribe — with role-scoped delegation, clean handoffs, and per-role model selection. This is value-feature #3 of the 7 capability features (design §1.2, RATIFY-1 / L1).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/README.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/README.md:21:## Overview
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/README.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/README.md:23:`agents` is gobbi's delegation system and agent roster: the per-role templates, Load Directives, status contract, model selection, and spawn topology that let a manager dispatch scoped work to fresh single-purpose subagents.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/README.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/README.md:25:## Status
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/README.md:26:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/README.md:27:Active. The 5-role agent roster (`agents/*.md`) and the `delegation` skill (per-role templates, Load Directives, status contract, model selection, spawn topology) are live. Durable agents-scope artifacts re-homed into this feature dir during the memory-system redesign.
