.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/backlogs/lock2-shared-executor-mega-task-risk.md:14:supersedes: null
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/backlogs/lock2-shared-executor-mega-task-risk.md:15:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/backlogs/lock2-shared-executor-mega-task-risk.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/backlogs/lock2-shared-executor-mega-task-risk.md:17:# Shared-executor context-budget risk (LOCK #2)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/backlogs/lock2-shared-executor-mega-task-risk.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/backlogs/lock2-shared-executor-mega-task-risk.md:19:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/backlogs/lock2-shared-executor-mega-task-risk.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/backlogs/lock2-shared-executor-mega-task-risk.md:21:LOCK #2 binds Tasks 07 (hook script) and Task 08 (reconstructor) into a single executor delegation back-to-back. The combined brief covers: bash strict-mode, flock -x, jq two-tier extraction, PostToolUse/PostToolUseFailure stdin contract, structured-header regex parsing, session.json upsert, D-3-3-resolver step (ii), PLUS the full reconstructor (idempotency, orphan-report, transcript-replay). Both are Large effort tasks.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/backlogs/lock2-shared-executor-mega-task-risk.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/backlogs/lock2-shared-executor-mega-task-risk.md:23:Risk: combined effort may exceed a single executor's context coherence budget, producing a partial implementation or quality regression on the second task (reconstructor).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/backlogs/lock2-shared-executor-mega-task-risk.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/backlogs/lock2-shared-executor-mega-task-risk.md:25:## Why deferred
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/backlogs/lock2-shared-executor-mega-task-risk.md:26:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/backlogs/lock2-shared-executor-mega-task-risk.md:27:LOCK #2 was user-confirmed. The rationale is valid: Tasks 07 and 08 share jq snippets and the hook stdin contract; splitting them into separate delegations would require the second executor to re-derive or re-fetch that context. The user weighed the tradeoff and accepted the shared-executor pattern.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/backlogs/lock2-shared-executor-mega-task-risk.md:28:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/backlogs/lock2-shared-executor-mega-task-risk.md:29:The risk is pre-existing — it was not introduced by the planning fix pass — and remains a probable-but-unverified concern rather than an observed failure.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/backlogs/lock2-shared-executor-mega-task-risk.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/backlogs/lock2-shared-executor-mega-task-risk.md:31:## When to pick up
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/backlogs/lock2-shared-executor-mega-task-risk.md:32:
