.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/ci-symlink-backlog-pseudocode-plumbing.md:14:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/ci-symlink-backlog-pseudocode-plumbing.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/ci-symlink-backlog-pseudocode-plumbing.md:16:# CI symlink integrity check — wrong git command in pseudocode
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/ci-symlink-backlog-pseudocode-plumbing.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/ci-symlink-backlog-pseudocode-plumbing.md:18:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/ci-symlink-backlog-pseudocode-plumbing.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/ci-symlink-backlog-pseudocode-plumbing.md:20:The project-level `ci-symlink-integrity-check.md` backlog file includes pseudocode for a pre-commit hook that guards the `.claude/`↔project symlink layer against accidental dereferencing. That pseudocode uses `git ls-files -s` for both the old-mode and staged-mode checks. However, `git ls-files -s` returns the staged (index) mode, not the HEAD/last-commit mode — so comparing staged to itself would never detect the `120000 → 100644` transition (a symlink silently replaced by a regular file). The integrity check, as written, cannot fire on the very failure mode it exists to catch.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/ci-symlink-backlog-pseudocode-plumbing.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/ci-symlink-backlog-pseudocode-plumbing.md:22:## Why deferred
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/ci-symlink-backlog-pseudocode-plumbing.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/ci-symlink-backlog-pseudocode-plumbing.md:24:Accepted as non-blocking: the integrity-check backlog itself is deferred (it has zero current witnesses — no CI symlink breakage has been observed — so Principle 10 keeps it un-built). The pseudocode is already labeled "Pseudocode — exact diff plumbing depends on the chosen pre-commit framework," so the wrong-command error is contained inside a not-yet-implemented sketch. Fixing the plumbing only matters once someone implements the check, so the fix is carried as a note on the deferred parent rather than acted on now.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/ci-symlink-backlog-pseudocode-plumbing.md:25:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/ci-symlink-backlog-pseudocode-plumbing.md:26:## When to pick up
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/ci-symlink-backlog-pseudocode-plumbing.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/ci-symlink-backlog-pseudocode-plumbing.md:28:When the `ci-symlink-integrity-check` backlog is itself picked up and implemented. The plumbing must be corrected before the check ships — otherwise the guard is inert.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/ci-symlink-backlog-pseudocode-plumbing.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/ci-symlink-backlog-pseudocode-plumbing.md:30:## Suggested approach
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/ci-symlink-backlog-pseudocode-plumbing.md:31:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/ci-symlink-backlog-pseudocode-plumbing.md:32:Correct the old-mode detection to read the committed mode rather than the staged mode: use `git diff --cached --raw` (which reports both the old and new mode per path) or `git ls-tree HEAD <path>` for the committed mode versus `git ls-files --stage <path>` for the staged mode. Compare the two so a `120000 → 100644` transition is detected.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/ci-symlink-backlog-pseudocode-plumbing.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/ci-symlink-backlog-pseudocode-plumbing.md:34:## Originating session
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/ci-symlink-backlog-pseudocode-plumbing.md:35:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/ci-symlink-backlog-pseudocode-plumbing.md:36:`.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/`
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/ci-symlink-backlog-pseudocode-plumbing.md:37:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/ci-symlink-backlog-pseudocode-plumbing.md:38:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/ci-symlink-backlog-pseudocode-plumbing.md:39:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/ci-symlink-backlog-pseudocode-plumbing.md:40:- [`../../../backlogs/ci-symlink-integrity-check.md`](../../../backlogs/ci-symlink-integrity-check.md) — the project-level backlog whose pseudocode this entry corrects
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/ci-symlink-backlog-pseudocode-plumbing.md:41:
