.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:9:session: 2026-05-23-7ea62d36-e826-4ce6-9e90-9e948007b068
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:10:tags: [wrap-up, step-2-5, anchor-placement, orchestration]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:11:domain: docs-sync
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:12:title: "Wrap-up Step 2.5 anchor placement — new H3 after ### WORK discipline"
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:13:project: gobbi
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:14:supersedes: null
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:15:superseded_by: null
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:16:decision_status: accepted
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:17:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:19:# Wrap-up Step 2.5 anchor placement
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:21:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:23:The new Step 2.5 (prior-loop MEMORIZATION compliance check) needed a home in `wrap-up/SKILL.md`. The two candidate placements were: inside the WORK Phase procedure table (where the existing Steps are numbered table rows), or as a new H3 between that table and a later subsection. The procedure table summarizes each step as a terse row, so an inline "Step 2.5" would not have room for the step's full specification.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:25:## Decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:26:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:27:Land Step 2.5 as a new `### Step 2.5 — prior-loop MEMORIZATION compliance check` H3 inserted between the `### WORK discipline` H3 and the `## Staging → Project-memory routing` H2. The procedure-table Step 2 row gets a one-line "see § Step 2.5 below" pointer.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:28:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:29:## Rationale
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:31:1. The procedure tables in this skill tree summarize steps as terse rows; inserting "Step 2.5" inline would force every adjacent row's step number to be re-anchored.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:32:2. A self-contained H3 gives Step 2.5 the ~10-20 line surface it needs for inputs, scan procedure, gap table, classification, auto-backfill + collision policy, NEEDS_CONTEXT trigger, and gap-report destination.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:33:3. Placement after `### WORK discipline` keeps the discipline block adjacent to the procedure table.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:34:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:35:## Alternatives considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:36:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:37:- **Inline Step 2.5 as a procedure-table row.** Rejected: a table row cannot hold the step's full specification, and inserting a "2.5" row forces re-anchoring of every adjacent step number.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:38:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:39:## Consequences
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:40:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:41:`wrap-up/SKILL.md` carries Step 2.5 as a self-contained H3 between the WORK discipline block and the Staging → Project-memory routing section, with a pointer from the Step 2 procedure-table row. The decision was adopted in the Planning draft with no user challenge.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:42:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:43:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:44:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-anchor-placement.md:45:- `design/wrap-up-step-2-5-compliance-check.md` — the Step 2.5 specification this placement hosts.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:1:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:2:name: hook-bash-jq-stack
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:3:description: Hook authoring stack is bash + jq with two-tier extraction strategy — prefer rich transcript toolUseResult payload, fall back to stdin tool_result.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:4:type: design
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:5:scope: feature
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:6:feature: install-runtime
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:7:status: locked
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:8:created: 2026-05-23
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:9:session: 1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:10:tags: [hooks, bash, jq, authoring-stack]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:11:design-id: D-3-1
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:12:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:13:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:14:# Hook authoring stack: bash + jq, two-tier extraction
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:16:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:18:The `post-tool-use-agents.sh` hook must extract subagent telemetry and write it into `session.json.agents[]`. The question was which language stack to author it in, and how to read the payload robustly against schema drift in the transcript format. The repo already has one hook precedent (`session-start.sh`) authored in bash + jq, and jq is already a hard dependency.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:20:## Decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:22:The `.claude/hooks/post-tool-use-agents.sh` hook is authored in bash + jq, modeled on `.claude/hooks/session-start.sh` (the existing precedent):
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:23:- Strict mode: `set -euo pipefail`
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:24:- Writability + nonempty guards
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:25:- `@sh` shell-safe quoting for jq string interpolation
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:26:- Defensive `// "fallback"` for forward-compat on every field extraction
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:28:**Two-tier extraction strategy**:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:29:1. Prefer rich `toolUseResult` payload from the transcript JSONL (full telemetry: `agentId`, `usage.*`, `totalDurationMs`, `toolStats`)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:30:2. Fall back to documented `tool_result` from hook stdin (minimal but stable public surface)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:31:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:32:The `flock` serialization step (see `flock-serialization-on-session-json.md`) is a mandatory step before any read in both hook and reconstructor.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:34:## Rationale
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:35:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:36:`session-start.sh` is the established bash+jq precedent; jq is already a hard dependency. Two-tier extraction mitigates forward-compat risk (schema drift) without leaving the bash+jq layer. No new runtime dependency; flock(1) is available on every Linux/macOS host.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:37:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:38:Supporting evidence anchored at decision time: the `session-start.sh` precedent (bash+jq established), the schema-drift forward-compat rationale, the two-tier extraction rationale, and the companion flock serialization design (`flock-serialization-on-session-json.md`).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:39:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:40:## Alternatives considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:41:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:42:- Node / Python — rejected: new runtime deps; break precedent.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:43:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:44:## Consequences
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:45:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:46:- The hook script (`post-tool-use-agents.sh`) is authored in bash + jq with the strict-mode + guards + `@sh` quoting + defensive-fallback contract above.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:47:- Validation obligations: an evaluator Consistency check (matching shebang + `set -euo pipefail`); a single-script verifier on a fixture transcript; a concurrent-fire smoke test (shared with the flock serialization design).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:48:- No new runtime dependency is introduced; future hook authors follow the same bash + jq stack.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:49:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:50:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:51:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:52:- `flock-serialization-on-session-json.md` — the mandatory serialization step before any read.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/hook-bash-jq-stack.md:53:- `metadata-extraction-input-vs-result.md` — the input-vs-result extraction split this stack feeds.
