.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/task01-t1c-trace-overclaim.md:26:### 1. Align `traces-to` with the actual file-map assignment
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/task01-t1c-trace-overclaim.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/task01-t1c-trace-overclaim.md:28:**Anchor reasoning**: novel — no reference governs trace accuracy; the rule is that a task only traces anchors whose edits it actually performs, so the trace stays an accurate audit link.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/task01-t1c-trace-overclaim.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/task01-t1c-trace-overclaim.md:30:### 2. Keep the heading consistent with `traces-to`
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/task01-t1c-trace-overclaim.md:31:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/task01-t1c-trace-overclaim.md:32:**Anchor reasoning**: novel — the heading must name the same anchors the trace does, or post-execution audit reads a stale label.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/task01-t1c-trace-overclaim.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/task01-t1c-trace-overclaim.md:34:Low severity — the executor reads `traces-to:` fields and the task `what`, not the heading, so the heading mismatch is cosmetic. Accurate `traces-to` fields still matter for post-execution audit (linking what was implemented to what was planned). This was out of the surgical fix scope when surfaced; carry it to a future plan revision or fix it in Execution brief prep.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:1:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:2:name: wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:3:description: "Wrap-up Step 2.5 escalation default — hybrid auto-backfill + NEEDS_CONTEXT"
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:4:type: decisions
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:5:scope: feature
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:6:feature: workflow
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:7:status: active
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:8:created: 2026-05-23
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:9:session: 2026-05-23-7ea62d36-e826-4ce6-9e90-9e948007b068
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:10:tags: [wrap-up, step-2-5, escalation, orchestration]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:11:supersedes: null
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:12:superseded_by: null
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:13:decision_status: accepted
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:14:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:16:# Wrap-up Step 2.5 escalation default
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:18:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:20:When Wrap-up's Step 2.5 detects a prior-loop MEMORIZATION gap, it needs a default action: auto-backfill the gap, escalate via NEEDS_CONTEXT, or some hybrid. The manager surfaced this to the user as a question, because the right answer depends on whether the gap is routing-deterministic (safe to fill automatically) or requires a design/arbitration call (must go back to the user).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:22:## Decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:24:Use a hybrid escalation default: auto-backfill mechanical gaps, and NEEDS_CONTEXT for gaps that involve a design choice or decision. The user's words: "Auto-backfill and NEEDS_CONTEXT for design or decision."
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:25:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:26:- **Auto-backfill** when the gap is mechanical / routing-deterministic — e.g., a `scenario_gap` finding routes to `staging/scenarios/{slug}.md` deterministically per `evaluation/SKILL.md § Finding Metadata`. The assistant writes the staging file from the finding's content.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:27:- **NEEDS_CONTEXT** when the gap involves a design choice or decision — e.g., a `design_flaw` finding that flags a routing ambiguity, a finding with `disposition: open` requiring user arbitration, or a finding that spans multiple staging subdirs and needs the user to pick the canonical destination.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:28:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:29:## Rationale
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:31:A routing-deterministic gap has exactly one valid destination, so escalating it to the user is pure friction; auto-backfill is safe and faster. A gap that needs a design call or arbitration has no single correct fill, so auto-backfilling it would make an autonomous choice the user must own. The hybrid splits cleanly along that line.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:32:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:33:## Alternatives considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:34:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:35:- **Always NEEDS_CONTEXT.** Rejected: too friction-heavy for gaps that route deterministically.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:36:- **Always auto-backfill.** Rejected: too autonomous on findings that require user arbitration.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:37:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:38:## Consequences
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:39:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:40:The Step 2.5 specification must classify each detected gap as `mechanical` or `judgment-required`, auto-fill the mechanical gaps inline, aggregate the judgment-required gaps into a single NEEDS_CONTEXT surfacing, and document the classification rules in `wrap-up/SKILL.md` so users can audit the assistant's gap-classification.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:41:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:42:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:43:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:44:- `design/wrap-up-step-2-5-compliance-check.md` — the Step 2.5 specification that implements this policy.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:45:- `discussions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-shape.md` — the AskUserQuestion exchange that selected the hybrid shape.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:46:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:47:## Source
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/wrap-up-step-2-5-escalation-default.md:48:
