.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-readability.md:8:created: 2026-05-23
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-readability.md:9:session: 1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-readability.md:10:tags: [dq-anchors, planning, checklist, readability]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-readability.md:11:domain: process
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-readability.md:12:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-readability.md:13:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-readability.md:14:# DQ-anchor readability — design questions defined in rawdata, not in the canonical draft
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-readability.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-readability.md:16:## What
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-readability.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-readability.md:18:The design questions for the T1 and T3 task waves are defined in the Ideation sub-step-D rawdata file but only referenced by anchor name in the canonical draft. A reader of the canonical draft alone cannot resolve a design-question anchor back to its question text without opening the sub-step rawdata file. The checklist item for Planning: before decomposing the T1/T3 tasks, read the sub-step-D rawdata to resolve the anchor meanings rather than re-deriving the questions from anchor names; optionally, if Planning builds a DQ index (see the sibling `dq-anchor-traceability.md`), copy the question text from rawdata into that index for cross-session discoverability.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-readability.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-readability.md:20:## Why
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-readability.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-readability.md:22:A Codex Aesthetics evaluation flagged that anchor-name-only references make the canonical draft unreadable in isolation — the reader has to chase the question text into a separate rawdata file. Resolving the anchors at Planning time prevents the decomposition from acting on misremembered question text.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-readability.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-readability.md:24:## Verification
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-readability.md:25:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-readability.md:26:Planning has read the sub-step-D rawdata and decomposed the T1/T3 tasks against the resolved question text (not anchor names alone); if a DQ index was created, it carries the question text inline.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-readability.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-readability.md:28:## Status notes
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-readability.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-readability.md:30:Adding the design-question text directly to the canonical draft was deferred because the authorized fix scope at the time was limited to a specific set of fixes; DQ readability improvements were out of that scope. Status: open — for Planning to act on at decomposition.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-readability.md:31:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-readability.md:32:## Source
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-readability.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-readability.md:34:Ideation evaluation (Codex Aesthetics) and the design-question source of truth are preserved in the originating session: `sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/rawdata/sub-step-d-design-iter1.md`.
