.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/mirror-policy-empirical-verification.md:13:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/mirror-policy-empirical-verification.md:14:# Mirror-policy empirical verification — implementation checklist
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/mirror-policy-empirical-verification.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/mirror-policy-empirical-verification.md:16:The empirical checks that must pass before the mirror-canonical policy (mirror file is canonical, the `.claude/` workspace is a symlink runtime layer) is locked. Each row was run and confirmed before the policy was accepted.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/mirror-policy-empirical-verification.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/mirror-policy-empirical-verification.md:18:| # | Item | Anchor | Status | Verification |
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/mirror-policy-empirical-verification.md:19:|---|---|---|---|---|
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/mirror-policy-empirical-verification.md:20:| 1 | Run file-level symlink scan before locking mirror-canonical policy | mirror-policy evaluation (Codex Consistency) | implemented | `find .claude/skills/ -type l -name "*.md" \| wc -l` → 53 |
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/mirror-policy-empirical-verification.md:21:| 2 | Verify sample symlink target resolves to canonical mirror file | mirror-policy evaluation | implemented | `ls -la .claude/skills/orchestration/SKILL.md` → symlink to `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/orchestration/SKILL.md` |
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/mirror-policy-empirical-verification.md:22:| 3 | Verify `git ls-files -s` mode is 120000 for workspace symlinks | empirical check | implemented | mode 120000 confirmed for `.claude/skills/orchestration/SKILL.md` |
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/mirror-policy-empirical-verification.md:23:| 4 | Reproduce symlink-replacement failure mode with unsafe edit tool | empirical check | implemented | `sed -i` against `/tmp` symlink confirms: link.md → regular file; canonical unchanged |
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/mirror-policy-empirical-verification.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/mirror-policy-empirical-verification.md:25:## Item details
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/mirror-policy-empirical-verification.md:26:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/mirror-policy-empirical-verification.md:27:### 1. File-level symlink scan
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/mirror-policy-empirical-verification.md:28:A directory-level scan misses file-level symlinks. The file-level (`-type l`) scan is the one that establishes how many workspace files are symlinks (53 here) before any policy assumes the topology.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/mirror-policy-empirical-verification.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/mirror-policy-empirical-verification.md:30:### 4. Reproduce the symlink-replacement failure mode
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/mirror-policy-empirical-verification.md:31:The failure mode is a rewrite-by-rename edit method (e.g. `sed -i`) silently replacing a symlink with a regular file. Reproducing it against a throwaway `/tmp` symlink confirms the hazard is real (the link becomes a regular file while the canonical target is untouched), which is what motivates the symlink-preservation edit contract.
