.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/hook-latency-bounds.md:11:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/hook-latency-bounds.md:12:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/hook-latency-bounds.md:13:# Hook and reconstructor latency bounds — Execution measurement
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/hook-latency-bounds.md:14:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/hook-latency-bounds.md:15:## What
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/hook-latency-bounds.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/hook-latency-bounds.md:17:At Execution, measure the PostToolUse hook's wall-clock cost against representative fixture transcripts (500, 1000, and 5000 lines) and verify it stays under 500ms p99 per fire. If any fixture exceeds 500ms p99, escalate to Planning for a latency-budget decision before shipping the hook.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/hook-latency-bounds.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/hook-latency-bounds.md:19:## Why
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/hook-latency-bounds.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/hook-latency-bounds.md:21:The hook's per-fire cost is O(transcript_lines) for the transcript scan, bounded by N Task spawns × session transcript size (typically 20-50 fires and under 5000 lines per session, with no external network call). No hard latency budget was locked at design time, so the per-fire cost is bounded only by analysis, not by a measured ceiling. A fixture measurement at Execution turns the assumed bound into a verified one before the hook fires on every real Task spawn.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/hook-latency-bounds.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/hook-latency-bounds.md:23:## Verification
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/hook-latency-bounds.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/hook-latency-bounds.md:25:Run the hook against the three fixture sizes, record wall-clock time, and confirm < 500ms p99 per fire. Failing that threshold gates the ship.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/hook-latency-bounds.md:26:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/hook-latency-bounds.md:27:## Status notes
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/hook-latency-bounds.md:28:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/hook-latency-bounds.md:29:Pending — the measurement runs at Execution time, once the hook script exists. No budget has been locked yet; the 500ms p99 figure above is the proposed gate, subject to the Planning escalation if a fixture exceeds it.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/hook-latency-bounds.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/hook-latency-bounds.md:31:## Source
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/hook-latency-bounds.md:32:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/checklists/hook-latency-bounds.md:33:Surfaced as a performance finding during install-runtime design evaluation (session 1b26cf20); the Codex evaluator flagged the absence of a hard latency budget at design time.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/backlogs/privacy-retention-agents-metadata-deferred.md:1:---
