.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:9:session: 1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:10:tags: [hook, flock, error-logging, failure-budget, planning]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:11:disposition: open
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:12:supersedes: null
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:13:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:14:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:15:# Hook self-failure budget — flock timeout and error logging left unstated
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:17:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:19:The hook script (`post-tool-use-agents.sh`) is invoked on PostToolUseFailure. If the hook itself fails (e.g., jq not available, flock timeout, session.json write permission denied), the failure is silent from Claude Code's perspective — Claude Code does not crash on hook errors.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:21:The plan does not specify: (1) what flock timeout to use, (2) whether hook errors should be logged, (3) what happens to `agents[]` if the hook silently fails for N consecutive Task spawns.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:23:## Why deferred
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:25:The hook's failure-recovery design is an Execution concern: the executor authoring the script can make appropriate choices for flock timeout and error logging based on the script's final structure, so locking those values in advance would over-specify. The risk is also bounded — the `reconstruct-agents.sh` script is the recovery mechanism for missed entries (it exists precisely to handle hook gaps, and is documented as "orphan-report-only (never deletes)" and the "hook crash/gap recovery mechanism"), so a silently-failed hook fire is recoverable rather than data-losing.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:26:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:27:## When to pick up
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:28:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:29:If the hook fails silently during a test after Execution. At that point, specify the three things the plan currently leaves open: (1) the flock timeout, (2) whether hook errors are logged, and (3) what happens to `agents[]` after N consecutive silent failures.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:31:## Suggested approach
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:32:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:33:Add an explicit flock timeout (`flock -x -w N`) and stderr-based error logging to the script so a hook self-failure is observable rather than silent. Record any observed failure mode as a mistake so the budget is grounded in a real witness rather than guessed.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:34:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:35:## Originating session
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:36:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:37:`.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/`
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:38:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:39:## Source
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/hook-self-failure-budget-unstated.md:40:
