.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:1:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:2:name: shared-executor-context-continuity
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:3:description: User decision to delegate Tasks 07 and 08 (hook script + reconstructor) to a single executor within one context window, preserving jq snippet continuity.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:4:type: discussions
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:5:scope: feature
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:6:feature: agents
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:7:status: active
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:8:created: 2026-05-24
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:9:session: 1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:10:tags: [delegation, executor, task-bundling, jq, hook]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:11:outcome: Single executor delegation confirmed; back-to-back within one context window
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:12:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:13:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:14:# Hook-script and reconstructor share one executor
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:16:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:18:The hook-script task and the reconstructor task share the same `jq` snippets and the same hook-stdin contract. The leader proposed bundling them into a single executor delegation so the shared context (the `jq` snippets, the stdin shape) does not have to be re-derived between two separate executors.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:20:## Question
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:22:Should the hook-script task and the reconstructor task be delegated to a single executor (back-to-back, one context window) or to two separate executors?
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:24:## Options considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:25:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:26:1. **Single delegation** — one executor handles the hook script first, then the reconstructor, within the same context window. Pros: `jq` snippet continuity; no re-derivation of the stdin contract. Cons: the combined effort (two large tasks) may stress the executor's context-coherence budget.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:27:2. **Separate delegations** — the reconstructor executor re-derives the snippets or receives an explicit `jq`-snippet handoff in its brief. Pros: bounded scope per delegation. Cons: risk that the reconstructor diverges from the hook script's established patterns if the handoff is imperfect.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:28:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:29:## User decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:31:The user confirmed the **single-executor delegation**: both tasks go to one executor, back-to-back within one context window.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:32:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:33:## Implication
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:34:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:35:The manager issues ONE delegation prompt covering both tasks. The executor completes the hook script first (producing the hook-script artifact, the shared `jq` snippets, and the hook-stdin contract), then the reconstructor (consuming those outputs).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:36:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:37:If context saturation occurs partway through the reconstructor, the manager can re-delegate the reconstructor as a fresh executor with the `jq` snippets from the hook-script output pasted in as literal brief context.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:38:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:39:## Source
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:40:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:41:Session 1b26cf20 planning — agent-assignment decision bundling the hook-script and reconstructor tasks under one executor.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:42:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:43:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/discussions/2026-05-24-shared-executor-context-continuity.md:44:
