.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-traceability.md:11:domain: process
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-traceability.md:12:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-traceability.md:13:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-traceability.md:14:# DQ-anchor traceability — no stand-alone DQ index, only local trace
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-traceability.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-traceability.md:16:## What
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-traceability.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-traceability.md:18:The design decisions in the canonical draft cite design-question anchors inline, but there is no stand-alone DQ index document cross-referencing each design question to its resolution. The checklist item for Planning: if a DQ index is needed for decomposition, add a cross-referencing index (design-question anchor → design-decision slug) — optional if Planning can navigate inline from the draft. Planning must NOT re-open any design question already answered in the draft's Decisions Log; the anchors are read-only from Planning onwards.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-traceability.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-traceability.md:20:## Why
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-traceability.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-traceability.md:22:A Codex Overall + Consistency evaluation flagged that the inline-only references give sufficient local trace for Planning but leave a cross-session discoverability gap: a future reader cannot find a single map from question to resolution. A DQ index would close that gap if the decomposition needs it.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-traceability.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-traceability.md:24:## Verification
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-traceability.md:25:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-traceability.md:26:Either Planning navigated the design questions inline from the draft (no index needed), or a DQ index exists cross-referencing each design-question anchor to its design-decision slug; no answered design question was re-opened.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-traceability.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-traceability.md:28:## Status notes
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-traceability.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-traceability.md:30:A formal DQ traceability document was scoped out at the time (the authorized scope was a specific fix set only). Status: open — this item surfaces the gap for Planning to decide whether a DQ index is worth creating before decomposition.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-traceability.md:31:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-traceability.md:32:## Source
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-traceability.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/checklists/dq-anchor-traceability.md:34:The Codex Overall and Consistency findings and the draft's Decisions Log are preserved in the originating session: `sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/rawdata/draft-iter3.md`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:1:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:2:name: memorization-delegation-hard-gate
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:3:description: Design decision to add a hard-gate Load Directive requiring memorization/SKILL.md in every delegation that includes a MEMORIZATION phase, preventing the pathology where the assistant runs Memorization without the staging procedure loaded.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:4:type: design
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:5:scope: feature
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:6:feature: agents
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:7:status: active
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:8:created: 2026-05-23
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:9:session: 7ea62d36-e826-4ce6-9e90-9e948007b068
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:10:tags: [memorization, delegation, load-directives, hard-gate]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:11:topic: memorization-delegation-hard-gate
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:12:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:13:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:14:# Memorization Delegation Hard Gate
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:16:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:18:A delegation prompt's Load Directives block names the skills a spawned agent must load before working — a fresh agent does not inherit the parent's loaded skills. The assistant role runs the MEMORIZATION phase, whose staging procedure lives in `memorization/SKILL.md`. The pathology this design addresses: delegation prompts that included a MEMORIZATION phase were not always listing `memorization/SKILL.md` in their Load Directives, so the assistant ran Memorization without the staging procedure loaded and improvised the staging step.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:20:## Decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:22:Add a hard-gate entry to `delegation/SKILL.md § The Load Directives Block` stating: "When the delegated phase includes MEMORIZATION (every loop's MEMORIZATION sub-phase, plus Wrap-up's WORK promotion routing), `memorization/SKILL.md` MUST appear in tier 3 (Skills)." Propagate the requirement into the per-role templates under `delegation/templates/`: the assistant template lists it explicitly; the leader and executor templates list it when MEMORIZATION is part of their dispatch. The evaluator template is excluded — evaluators do not run MEMORIZATION.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:24:## Rationale
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:25:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:26:The requirement is enforced at the delegation-contract level rather than left to the agent's discretion: if a skill is in Load Directives, it is loaded; no internal self-check saves an agent that was never given the directive. Making the gate part of the prompt-construction contract closes the gap at the point where the prompt is authored, which is where the omission originated.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:28:## Alternatives considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:30:- **Self-check inside the assistant's MEMORIZATION procedure Step 1** ("did I load `memorization/SKILL.md`?"). Rejected as duplicative and unreliable — if Load Directives already include the skill, the check is redundant; if they do not, no internal check can load a skill the dispatch never named.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:31:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:32:## Consequences
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:34:- Every delegation that includes a MEMORIZATION phase now carries `memorization/SKILL.md` in its Load Directives, so the staging procedure is always loaded before Memorization runs.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:35:- Verify with `grep -c "memorization/SKILL.md" delegation/SKILL.md` (expect ≥ 2) and confirm each relevant per-role template includes `memorization/SKILL.md` in its Skills example.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/memorization-delegation-hard-gate.md:36:- Cross-reference: `delegation/SKILL.md § Load Directives` / Core Principles point at `memorization/SKILL.md § Procedure`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:1:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:2:name: sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:3:description: Deferred hardening — use session.json.lock sidecar instead of locking session.json directly
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:4:type: backlogs
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:5:scope: feature
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:6:feature: install-runtime
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:7:status: active
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:8:created: 2026-05-23
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:9:session: 1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:10:tags: [flock, locking, sidecar, session-json, hardening]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:11:disposition: open
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:12:supersedes: null
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:13:superseded_by: null
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:14:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:16:# Sidecar lock file refinement — flock on session.json.lock vs session.json directly
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:18:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:20:The PostToolUse hook acquires `flock -x` on `session.json` itself rather than on a separate `session.json.lock` sidecar file. Locking the file being mutated works (POSIX `flock(1)` locks on the file descriptor), and it addresses the primary lost-update race: two concurrent PostToolUse hooks clobbering each other's `agents[]` append. A dedicated sidecar would be a cleaner separation of concerns — the lock file would have a known lifecycle independent of the data file's atomic-rename cycle — but it is a refinement, not a correctness fix.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:22:## Why deferred
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:24:The primary race is fully addressed by the current locking design, so the sidecar is hardening rather than correctness. The one concern a sidecar would address — if the hook used `mv` (atomic rename), a new inode would get a new file descriptor and the old lock fd would go stale — does not apply to the current implementation, which uses an `exec {fd}>>"$session_json"; flock -x "$fd"` pattern that holds the same fd open through the write cycle. With the inode concern moot, the sidecar adds no correctness value today.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:25:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:26:## When to pick up
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:28:When the flock design is revisited for any reason — for example a new concurrent-access edge case, or a change to the atomic-write pattern. In particular, if the executor's atomic-write implementation ever deviates from the fd-based pattern (e.g. switches to rewrite-by-rename), the stale-fd concern returns and the sidecar becomes worth adding.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:30:## Suggested approach
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:31:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:32:Switch the lock target from `session.json` to a dedicated `session.json.lock` sidecar: acquire `flock -x` on the sidecar fd, perform the read-modify-write on `session.json` under that lock, and never tie the lock's lifecycle to the data file's inode. This survives a rewrite-by-rename write pattern.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:34:## Originating session
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:35:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:36:`.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/`
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:37:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:38:## Source
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:39:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred.md:40:Surfaced as a structure/risk finding during install-runtime design evaluation (session 1b26cf20); deferred as non-blocking hardening since the fd-based locking pattern already addresses the primary race.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:1:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:2:name: schema-extension-agents-status-field
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:3:description: session.template.json agents[] status field — deferred formal schema extension
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:4:type: backlogs
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:5:scope: feature
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:6:feature: install-runtime
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:7:project: gobbi
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:8:status: active
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:9:created: 2026-05-23
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:10:session: 1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:11:tags: [schema, session-template, agents, status-field, deferred]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:12:disposition: open
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:13:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:14:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:15:# `session.template.json` agents[] status field — formal schema extension deferred
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:17:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:19:The PostToolUse hook is registered for both `PostToolUse` and `PostToolUseFailure` events. Failed Task spawns produce an `agents[]` entry with `status: "failed"` and a synthetic `id` (= `tool_use_id`). However, the current `session.template.json.agents[]` element schema does NOT formally include a `status` field — the template implies happy-path entries only.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:21:The hook implementation writes the `status` field as an extra-property (the runtime JSON merging is permissive) without bumping the template schema. The formal template extension to officially accept `status: "failed"` (and a complementary `status: "success"` for symmetry) is deferred to keep the originating session's PR scope at docs + hook + script level.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:23:## Why deferred
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:25:User-confirmed deferral at design-decision lock time. Reasons:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:26:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:27:- Template bump would require a schema version increment and migration of any in-flight `session.json` files.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:28:- Scope discipline — the originating session's PR is already touching ~10 doc files + 2 new shell scripts + 1 `settings.json` edit. Adding template + migration would balloon scope.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:29:- The "extra-property" approach is forward-compatible: future template versions can add `status` formally without breaking existing entries.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:31:## When to pick up
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:32:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:33:- At any future session that revisits the `session.template.json` schema.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:34:- When the next feature requires bumping `session.template.json` schema for any other reason (bundle the changes).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:35:- If an evaluator perspective flags the "extra-property" as a contract-violation concern.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:36:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:37:## Suggested approach
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:38:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:39:Small in effort — a single template edit plus a version bump plus a couple of small doc updates:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:40:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:41:1. Bump `session.template.json` schemaVersion.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:42:2. Add `status: <string, enum [success, failed]>` to the `agents[]` element schema.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:43:3. Update the hook + reconstructor scripts to write `status` formally (no logic change — they already write the field).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:44:4. Migration: existing sessions without the field are accepted as legacy; new sessions stamp `status: "success"` by default.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:45:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:46:## Originating session
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:47:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:48:`.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/`
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:49:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:50:## Source
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:51:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/backlogs/schema-extension-agents-status-field.md:52:Surfaced from the dual-event hook scope design decision (the hook is registered for both `PostToolUse` and `PostToolUseFailure`, so failed spawns produce a `status: "failed"` audit-trail entry). The formal schema extension was a user-confirmed deferral at design-decision lock time.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:1:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:2:name: execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:3:description: Mandatory boilerplate every manager must include in every executor task brief — symlink-edit contract, mistake load directives, branch naming, commit trailers.
