.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:13:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:14:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:15:# Execution intake notes — cross-cutting requirements
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:17:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:19:When a manager delegates work into the Execution loop, each executor task brief needs the same handful of cross-cutting requirements: how to edit symlinked workspace files without breaking the symlink, which mistakes to load, how to name the branch, and how to stamp commits. These are not per-task decisions — they are standing conventions that apply to every executor delegation. Without a single home for them, each manager re-derives the same boilerplate (and occasionally omits a load-bearing piece, such as the symlink-preservation contract or a required mistake-load directive), causing repeat failures the project has already paid for once.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:21:## Decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:23:Every executor task brief MUST embed the following cross-cutting requirements as mandatory boilerplate. They are listed here once so the manager copies them into each brief rather than reinventing them.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:25:### Edit-tool default for `.claude/skills/` workspace paths
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:26:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:27:The `.claude/skills/` workspace paths are symlinks resolving to the canonical mirror under `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/`. To avoid breaking the symlink:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:28:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:29:- **Default**: use the Edit tool for every modification to a `.claude/skills/...` workspace path.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:30:- **Forbidden on workspace**: `sed -i`, `perl -i`, or any in-place stream editor that re-creates the file and replaces the symlink with a regular file.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:31:- **Bulk rewrites**: target the canonical mirror `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/...` directly rather than the workspace symlink.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:32:- **Post-edit verification gate**: run `test -L .claude/skills/<path>`. A non-zero exit means the symlink was broken and must be restored.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:33:- **Restore command** (empirically verified 2026-05-24): `rm -f .claude/skills/<path> && ln -sfn ../../../.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/<path> .claude/skills/<path>`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:34:- **Depth disclaimer**: use `../../../` for a `SKILL.md` directly under `.claude/skills/<topic>/`, and `../../../../` for files one level deeper. Always verify the relative depth against an adjacent untouched symlink with `ls -la`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:35:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:36:### Mistake load directives
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:37:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:38:Briefs that create or move session/worktree files must load the worktree-safety and verbatim-spec-recheck mistakes so the executor avoids the cwd-reset, rm-rf, and spec-drift traps the project has already hit:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:39:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:40:```
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:41:.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:42:.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/manager-rm-rf-without-investigating-tracked-files.md
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:43:.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/manager-iter2-brief-failed-iron-law-7-verbatim-spec-recheck.md
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:44:```
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:45:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:46:Briefs for lighter procedural tasks (script edits, small additions) load at minimum the verbatim-spec-recheck mistake:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:47:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:48:```
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:49:.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/manager-iter2-brief-failed-iron-law-7-verbatim-spec-recheck.md
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:50:```
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:51:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:52:### Branch naming convention
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:53:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:54:The session branch is `chore/session-{date}-{ssid-short}`. The manager creates it at session bootstrap (the worktree-create config step); executors never create the branch — they commit onto the branch the manager already prepared.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:55:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:56:### Per-iteration commit subject
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:57:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:58:`chore(session): record <loop> iter{n} memory`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:59:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:60:### AI-Provenance-Record trailer
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:61:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:62:Every commit emitted by Execution MUST carry the provenance trailer:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:63:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:64:```
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:65:AI-Provenance-Record: gobbi://session/{ssid}/task/{task-id}
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:66:```
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:67:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:68:The trailer goes at the bottom of the commit message body, separated from the prose by a blank line. `{ssid}` is the full session ID; `{task-id}` is the planning task ID (for example, `01-orchestration-worktree-create`).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:69:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:70:### Shell-script syntax gate
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:71:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:72:For tasks that author or modify shell scripts:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:73:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:74:- `bash -n <script>` is ALWAYS run as the syntax gate (bash is universally available).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:75:- `shellcheck` is CONDITIONAL: run it only if `command -v shellcheck` succeeds. When `shellcheck` is absent, note the omission in the commit body ("shellcheck not available in this workspace; CI re-gate when available").
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:76:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:77:## Rationale
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:78:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:79:These requirements are collected in one design doc because each one encodes a failure the project already paid for: the symlink-edit contract prevents `sed -i` from silently converting a symlink into a regular file; the mistake-load directives front-load the cwd-reset and spec-recheck traps so a fresh executor does not rediscover them; the branch and trailer conventions keep every commit attributable and on the correct branch. Centralizing them means the manager copies a known-good block instead of reconstructing it (and risking omission) per delegation.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:80:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:81:## Alternatives considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:82:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:83:- **Leave the requirements implicit in each manager's judgment.** Rejected: implicit requirements are the exact failure mode that produced the symlink-break and wrong-branch-commit mistakes. A standing checklist is the cheaper insurance.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:84:- **Encode each requirement as a runtime validator instead of brief boilerplate.** Deferred: a Load-Directives validator is tracked separately (see the validator-scope discussion); until it exists, the boilerplate is the enforcement surface.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:85:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:86:## Consequences
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:87:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:88:- Every executor delegation prompt carries this block (or the relevant subset), so the manager's brief-construction step has a fixed source rather than per-session recall.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:89:- When a new cross-cutting requirement is discovered, it is added here once and inherited by all future briefs.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:90:- Adding a runtime validator later would let the manager reference this doc as the validator's rule source rather than re-specifying the rules.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:91:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:92:## Source
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:93:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/agents/design/execution-intake-notes-cross-cutting.md:94:Session 1b26cf20 Preparation — symlink-preservation policy and per-tier mistake-load directives established during the session-foundations-bundle-b planning. The restore command was empirically verified on 2026-05-24.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:1:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:2:name: non-feature-session-scope
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:3:description: User confirmed worktree-first applies uniformly to every session, not only feature sessions; direct mode is the opt-out.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:4:type: discussions
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:5:scope: feature
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:6:feature: git-workflow
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:7:status: active
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:8:created: 2026-05-23
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:9:session: 1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:10:tags: [git-workflow, worktree-first, session-scope, non-feature]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:11:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:12:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:13:# Non-feature session scope — worktree-first for every session (uniform)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:14:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:15:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:17:Worktree-first was being locked as the session architecture, but its reach was undecided: should it apply only to feature sessions (those tied to a GitHub issue), or to every session including investigation, doc-only, and mistake-promotion sessions that have no issue? The answer determines whether non-feature sessions get a worktree branch at all.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:19:## Question
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:21:Should worktree-first apply only to feature sessions, or uniformly to every session?
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:23:## Options considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:25:1. **Feature sessions only** — worktree-first applies when there is a GitHub issue; investigation / doc-only / mistake-promotion sessions run on the main tree as before.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:26:2. **Uniform** — worktree-first applies to every session; non-feature sessions get a session-infrastructure branch with no issue prefix, and direct mode is the opt-out for the rare session that needs the main tree.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:28:## User decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:30:User chose **uniform**: worktree-first for every session. Direct mode is preserved as the opt-out per Design Decision D-5.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:31:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:32:## Implication
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:34:Every session boots on a worktree branch. The non-feature branch name `chore/session-{date}-{ssid-short}` (no issue prefix) handles investigation and maintenance sessions. D-5 documents direct mode as the escape hatch for emergency hotfix or read-only sessions.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:35:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:36:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:37:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:38:- `design/direct-mode-retained-opt-out.md` — Design Decision D-5, the direct-mode opt-out that makes uniform worktree-first safe.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:39:- `design/worktree-create-before-session-stamp.md` — the worktree-creation step (D-1) and the non-feature branch-naming scheme.
