.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/promote-now-depends-on-worktree-first.md:12:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/promote-now-depends-on-worktree-first.md:13:# Promote-now commit-on-branch dependency on worktree-first confirmed
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/promote-now-depends-on-worktree-first.md:14:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/promote-now-depends-on-worktree-first.md:15:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/promote-now-depends-on-worktree-first.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/promote-now-depends-on-worktree-first.md:17:The session had four candidate items, one of which was a new "Preparation promote-now commit-on-branch" addition. Before scope could be locked, the session needed to know whether that addition was an independent task or a dependent of the worktree-first work — which determines whether it stands alone or is absorbed.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/promote-now-depends-on-worktree-first.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/promote-now-depends-on-worktree-first.md:19:## Question
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/promote-now-depends-on-worktree-first.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/promote-now-depends-on-worktree-first.md:21:Is the "Preparation promote-now commit-on-branch" item technically dependent on worktree-first, or can it ship independently?
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/promote-now-depends-on-worktree-first.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/promote-now-depends-on-worktree-first.md:23:## Options considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/promote-now-depends-on-worktree-first.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/promote-now-depends-on-worktree-first.md:25:1. **Dependent on worktree-first, absorbed into it** — promote-now needs a `$worktreePath` to commit to; without worktree-first there is no branch to commit on, so it collapses to a 2-line `git add` + `git commit` addition to `preparation/SKILL.md` once worktree-first is locked.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/promote-now-depends-on-worktree-first.md:26:2. **Independent task** — promote-now ships as its own Execution task standing apart from worktree-first.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/promote-now-depends-on-worktree-first.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/promote-now-depends-on-worktree-first.md:28:## User decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/promote-now-depends-on-worktree-first.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/promote-now-depends-on-worktree-first.md:30:Confirmed dependent on worktree-first. Without worktree-first there is no `$worktreePath` to commit to, so promote-now is a small addition on top of it rather than a standalone task.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/promote-now-depends-on-worktree-first.md:31:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/promote-now-depends-on-worktree-first.md:32:## Implication
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/promote-now-depends-on-worktree-first.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/promote-now-depends-on-worktree-first.md:34:The promote-now commit-on-branch feature is absorbed into the worktree-first Execution tasks rather than standing as its own task. It ships as part of the worktree-first session architecture. See `design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md` for the locked design.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/promote-now-depends-on-worktree-first.md:35:
