.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/branch-name-collision-recovery.md:14:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/branch-name-collision-recovery.md:15:# Branch name collision — `chore/session-{date}-{ssid-short}` already exists
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/branch-name-collision-recovery.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/branch-name-collision-recovery.md:17:**Category:** failure-mode
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/branch-name-collision-recovery.md:18:**Coverage:** uncovered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/branch-name-collision-recovery.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/branch-name-collision-recovery.md:20:## Situation
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/branch-name-collision-recovery.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/branch-name-collision-recovery.md:22:A prior session at the same date with the same 8-char ssid prefix left an existing branch (e.g., due to a resume case where the idempotency guard misfired, or a manual git branch creation). When the manager invokes row 5.5 for a new session, `git worktree add -b chore/session-{date}-{ssid-short}` fails with "branch already exists". Row 5.5 does not document this scenario; P2's collision handling is not explicitly confirmed to cover it.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/branch-name-collision-recovery.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/branch-name-collision-recovery.md:24:## Inputs
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/branch-name-collision-recovery.md:25:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/branch-name-collision-recovery.md:26:- `git.workflow.mode` is `worktree-pr`
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/branch-name-collision-recovery.md:27:- `session.json.git.worktreePath` is null (fresh session, not a resume)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/branch-name-collision-recovery.md:28:- A git branch `chore/session-{date}-{ssid-short}` already exists from a prior operation
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/branch-name-collision-recovery.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/branch-name-collision-recovery.md:30:## Expected behavior
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/branch-name-collision-recovery.md:31:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/branch-name-collision-recovery.md:32:Row 5.5 or P2 should define behavior: (a) verify P2 handles branch-exists collision gracefully, or (b) add a collision-detection branch to row 5.5 before invoking P2. Manager should not be stuck mid-Configuration with no documented recovery.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/branch-name-collision-recovery.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/branch-name-collision-recovery.md:34:## Verification
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/branch-name-collision-recovery.md:35:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/branch-name-collision-recovery.md:36:Read `git/SKILL.md` P2 (line 153+) to confirm whether P2 handles the branch-already-exists case. If P2 does not cover it, file a backlog item against P2 or against row 5.5.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/branch-name-collision-recovery.md:37:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/branch-name-collision-recovery.md:38:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/branch-name-collision-recovery.md:39:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/branch-name-collision-recovery.md:40:- `git/SKILL.md` P2 (Create worktree) — the invocation target whose branch-collision handling is unconfirmed.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/branch-name-collision-recovery.md:41:- Surfaced by a risk-evaluation finding during the worktree-first session-architecture work (session `1b26cf20`, 2026-05-24).
