.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:11:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:12:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:13:# Per-iteration session-memory commit subject — chore(session) confirmed
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:14:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:15:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:17:Design Decision D-4 commits session memory to the worktree branch once per iteration. The commit subject needed a Conventional-Commits scope token, and the choice was between scoping by the directory being committed (`session`) or by the workflow loop that produced the commit.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:19:## Question
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:21:What should the per-iteration session-memory commit subject be — scope by directory or by loop?
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:23:## Options considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:25:1. **`chore(session): record <loop> iter{n} memory`** — `session` as the scope token, matching the `sessions/` directory being committed; the loop name goes in the subject body.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:26:2. **`chore(<loop>): record iter{n} memory`** — the loop name as the scope token.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:28:## User decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:30:Confirmed option 1, `chore(session): record <loop> iter{n} memory` — the `session` scope matches the directory being committed; the loop name goes in the subject body.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:31:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:32:## Implication
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:34:Design Decision D-4's commit subject pattern is locked: `chore(session): record <loop> iter{n} memory` (e.g., `chore(session): record ideation iter3 memory`). All 5 workflow loop docs carry this pattern.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:35:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:36:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:37:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:38:- `design/per-iteration-session-commit-cadence.md` — Design Decision D-4, which adopts this subject pattern.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/per-iter-commit-subject-scope.md:39:- `design/workflow-phase-doc-set-for-per-iter-cadence.md` — the 5 loop docs that carry the pattern.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:1:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:2:name: session-memory-survival
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:3:description: User locked session dir in the worktree; PR squash absorbs it on merge. Session memory survives via per-iteration commits, not Wrap-up promotion.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:4:type: discussions
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:5:scope: feature
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:6:feature: git-workflow
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:7:status: active
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:8:created: 2026-05-23
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:9:session: 1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:10:tags: [git-workflow, session-dir, worktree-first, session-memory]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:11:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:12:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:13:# Session-memory survival — session dir lives in worktree, absorbed by PR squash
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:14:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:15:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:17:Under worktree-first the worktree is removed at Wrap-up, which raises the question of where the session directory lives and how its contents survive removal. Several placements were possible, each with different durability and merge behavior.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:19:## Question
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:21:Where should the session directory live under worktree-first, so its memory survives worktree removal?
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:23:## Options considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:25:1. **Wrap-up promotes session memory to the main tree before worktree removal** — survival via an explicit promotion step.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:26:2. **Session dir in the main tree (direct mode unchanged)** — the session dir never enters the worktree.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:27:3. **Session dir lives in the worktree; the PR squash absorbs it on merge** — the worktree carries the whole session dir, and merging the PR brings it into history.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:28:4. **Hybrid — session memory in the main tree, generated files in the worktree** — split across two trees.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:30:## User decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:31:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:32:User locked option 3 — the session dir lives in the worktree, and the PR squash absorbs it on merge. Options 1, 2, and 4 were rejected.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:34:## Implication
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:35:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:36:Every session-memory write (staging files, session.json, rawdata, evaluation, artifacts) goes into the worktree's `.gobbi/projects/<name>/sessions/<date>-<ssid>/` tree. The PR squash commit carries the entire session directory. This anchors Design Decision D-4: the per-iteration commit cadence ensures durability *before* the PR is created, so a mid-session abort does not lose memory even though the dir lives only in the worktree.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:37:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:38:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:39:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:40:- `design/per-iteration-session-commit-cadence.md` — Design Decision D-4, the per-iteration cadence that makes worktree-resident session memory durable.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/session-memory-survival.md:41:- `design/qualified-git-write-path-rule.md` — the write-path rule (D-2) that roots session writes at `worktreePath`.
