.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:14:# Hook scope: PostToolUse + PostToolUseFailure dual registration with session-dir resolver
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:16:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:18:The PostToolUse hook that populates `session.json.agents[]` must capture both successful and failed subagent spawns, and it must locate the correct `session.json` from only the fields the hook receives on stdin (`session_id`, `transcript_path`, `cwd`). Two questions had to be resolved: which hook events to register, and how the hook resolves the session directory at runtime.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:20:## Decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:22:Register both `PostToolUse` and `PostToolUseFailure` with matcher `"Task"` in `.claude/settings.json`; single script handles both (branches on `hook_event_name` / `status`). Failed-spawn entries get `status: "failed"` and synthetic `id` (= `tool_use_id`) when `agentId` is null.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:24:**Session-dir resolver algorithm:**
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:25:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:26:The hook stdin contains `session_id`, `transcript_path`, and `cwd`. The session.json path is at `$cwd/.gobbi/projects/<project-name>/sessions/{date}-<session_id>/session.json`. Resolver derives `<project-name>` and `{date}`:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:28:1. **Project name lookup precedence**:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:29:   - **(i — preferred)**: Read `$cwd/.gobbi/project.json` and extract `name` field if file exists.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:30:     - **DORMANT PRECONDITION**: this file does not exist today (verified 2026-05-23). The resolver always falls through to step (ii). Tracked in backlog: `dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:31:   - **(ii — fallback, currently only working path)**: Enumerate `$cwd/.gobbi/projects/`; select single directory if exactly one exists. If zero or multiple: `exit 1` with stderr `"session-dir resolver: cannot disambiguate project name (n=<count>)"`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:32:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:33:2. **Date prefix lookup**: Scan `$cwd/.gobbi/projects/<name>/sessions/` for a directory ending in `-<session_id>`; take its full name. If zero or multiple: `exit 1` with stderr `"session-dir resolver: cannot disambiguate session dir (n=<count>)"`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:34:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:35:3. Resolved path: `$cwd/.gobbi/projects/<name>/sessions/<full-dir-name>/session.json`. If file absent: `exit 1`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:36:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:37:## Official documentation (verbatim)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:38:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:39:`PostToolUseFailure` is officially documented at `https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks` (WebFetched 2026-05-23):
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:40:- Lifecycle table: `| PostToolUseFailure | After a tool call fails |`
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:41:- Exit-code-behavior table: `| PostToolUseFailure | No | Shows stderr to Claude (tool already failed) |`
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:42:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:43:## Rationale
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:44:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:45:Failed spawns are part of the audit trail. `PostToolUseFailure` is officially supported (verbatim quote from official docs confirms this). Single script maintains DRY. Resolver using `project.json` preferred + dir-scan fallback: canonical when present; robust fallback for single-project repos.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:46:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:47:Supporting evidence anchored at decision time: empirical verification of the PostToolUseFailure lifecycle; the official-docs verbatim quote (above); the project-resolver precedence rationale; and the PostToolUse hook schema reference under `references/`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:48:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:49:## Alternatives considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:50:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:51:- PostToolUse only — rejected: loses the failed-spawn audit trail.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:52:- Two scripts — rejected: DRY violation.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:53:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:54:## Consequences
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:55:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:56:- `.claude/settings.json` registers both `PostToolUse` and `PostToolUseFailure` with matcher `"Task"`, both pointing at the single script.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:57:- The session-dir resolver carries a dormant `project.json` precondition: `$cwd/.gobbi/project.json` does not exist today, so the resolver always falls through to the single-directory enumeration path. Bootstrapping that file is tracked in backlog `dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:58:- Validation obligations: a smoke test on an artificial spawn failure; an evaluator Risk-perspective review; and a verbatim-quote presence check in the staged reference file.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:59:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:60:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/dual-hook-registration-resolver.md:61:
