.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/no-issue-worktree-branch-bootstrap.md:14:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/no-issue-worktree-branch-bootstrap.md:15:# Non-feature session: no issue/task slug dependency at worktree creation
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/no-issue-worktree-branch-bootstrap.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/no-issue-worktree-branch-bootstrap.md:17:**Category:** edge-case
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/no-issue-worktree-branch-bootstrap.md:18:**Coverage:** covered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/no-issue-worktree-branch-bootstrap.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/no-issue-worktree-branch-bootstrap.md:20:## Situation
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/no-issue-worktree-branch-bootstrap.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/no-issue-worktree-branch-bootstrap.md:22:A session that is not associated with a GitHub issue or a task slug (e.g., investigation, mistake-promotion, doc-lookup, or refactor-only session) boots via `/gobbi`. Configuration Step 1 reaches the worktree-creation step and must create a worktree. Under a prior branch-naming proposal of `session/{date}-{ssid-short}`, the branch type `session/` was not in the `git/conventions.md` type registry. The locked form `chore/session-{date}-{ssid-short}` uses `chore`, which does not require an issue number.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/no-issue-worktree-branch-bootstrap.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/no-issue-worktree-branch-bootstrap.md:24:## Inputs
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/no-issue-worktree-branch-bootstrap.md:25:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/no-issue-worktree-branch-bootstrap.md:26:- Session started with `/gobbi` without a linked issue or task
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/no-issue-worktree-branch-bootstrap.md:27:- `session.json.git.issue` is null
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/no-issue-worktree-branch-bootstrap.md:28:- Row 5.5 is reached
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/no-issue-worktree-branch-bootstrap.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/no-issue-worktree-branch-bootstrap.md:30:## Expected behavior
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/no-issue-worktree-branch-bootstrap.md:31:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/no-issue-worktree-branch-bootstrap.md:32:The worktree-creation step creates a worktree on branch `chore/session-{date}-{ssid-short}` (e.g., `chore/session-2026-05-23-1b26cf20`). No issue-number prefix is expected or required. The branch name satisfies the `git/conventions.md` type regex for `chore/`, and the slug `session-...` satisfies the 3-50 char length constraint.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/no-issue-worktree-branch-bootstrap.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/no-issue-worktree-branch-bootstrap.md:34:## Verification
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/no-issue-worktree-branch-bootstrap.md:35:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/no-issue-worktree-branch-bootstrap.md:36:Post-merge smoke test: `jq '.git.branch' session.json` matches `^chore/session-[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}-[a-f0-9]{8}$`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/no-issue-worktree-branch-bootstrap.md:37:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/no-issue-worktree-branch-bootstrap.md:38:## Related
