.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/checklists/config-table-row-numbering-choice.md:13:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/checklists/config-table-row-numbering-choice.md:14:# Choose decimal-5.5 insertion vs renumbering rows 6+ in the Configuration table
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/checklists/config-table-row-numbering-choice.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/checklists/config-table-row-numbering-choice.md:16:## What
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/checklists/config-table-row-numbering-choice.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/checklists/config-table-row-numbering-choice.md:18:Before inserting the worktree-creation row into the `orchestration/SKILL.md` Step 1 Workflow Configuration table, choose ONE numbering approach:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/checklists/config-table-row-numbering-choice.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/checklists/config-table-row-numbering-choice.md:20:- **(a) Keep the decimal row 5.5** — acceptable if the table's purpose is reference (readers scan by semantic label, not row count); leaves existing rows numbered as-is; no follow-on renumbering required.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/checklists/config-table-row-numbering-choice.md:21:- **(b) Renumber rows 6 → 7, 7 → 8, etc.** — consistent with the integer-only convention; requires updating all cross-references to row numbers throughout the skill file and any file that references "row 6" or "row 7".
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/checklists/config-table-row-numbering-choice.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/checklists/config-table-row-numbering-choice.md:23:Document the chosen approach as a one-line rationale in the PR description.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/checklists/config-table-row-numbering-choice.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/checklists/config-table-row-numbering-choice.md:25:## Why
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/checklists/config-table-row-numbering-choice.md:26:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/checklists/config-table-row-numbering-choice.md:27:A structural evaluation surfaced that the Step 1 Workflow Configuration table uses integer row numbers (1 through 7+), while the worktree-create design inserts the new row as a half-decimal (5.5) between the existing row 5 (state.json) and row 6 (session.json). The project's existing tables do not use decimal row numbers anywhere verified, so the insertion needs a deliberate numbering decision rather than an unreviewed half-decimal.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/checklists/config-table-row-numbering-choice.md:28:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/checklists/config-table-row-numbering-choice.md:29:## Verification
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/checklists/config-table-row-numbering-choice.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/checklists/config-table-row-numbering-choice.md:31:After the edit, `grep -n 'row [0-9]' .claude/skills/orchestration/SKILL.md` confirms no stale integer references remain (if approach (b) was chosen) and the table reads consistently.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/checklists/config-table-row-numbering-choice.md:32:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/checklists/config-table-row-numbering-choice.md:33:## Status notes
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/checklists/config-table-row-numbering-choice.md:34:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/checklists/config-table-row-numbering-choice.md:35:The edit target is the `orchestration/SKILL.md` Step 1 Configuration table (its integer-numbered rows appear around lines 95-110). Surfaced by a Claude structural evaluation finding during the worktree-first session-architecture work (session `1b26cf20`).
