.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:13:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:14:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:15:# `$CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` absent — branch-name derivation fallback
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:17:**Category:** failure-mode
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:18:**Coverage:** uncovered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:20:## Situation
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:22:The manager is executing the Configuration Step 1 worktree-creation step in a Codex environment or a Claude Code build that does not inject `$CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`. The step specifies `{ssid-short} = first 8 characters of $CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` but does not define a fallback when the env var is absent or empty. The manager has no documented recovery path and would produce a trailing-hyphen branch name (`chore/session-YYYY-MM-DD-`) that fails the `git/conventions.md` shape regex.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:24:## Inputs
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:25:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:26:- `$CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` is empty/unset
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:27:- `git.workflow.mode` is `worktree-pr`
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:28:- Manager is following row 5.5 literally
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:30:## Expected behavior
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:31:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:32:The worktree-creation step should specify a fallback: if `$CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` is absent, derive `{ssid-short}` from `openssl rand -hex 4` (or equivalent) and proceed. This mirrors how the session-stamp step handles an absent `transcriptPath` by leaving it `null`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:34:## Verification
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:35:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:36:Confirm the worktree-creation prose (after a dedicated fix task or footnote addition) includes an explicit absent-env-var branch. Check that the `git/conventions.md` shape regex accepts the materialized branch name in both env-present and env-absent scenarios.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:37:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:38:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:39:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:40:- `git/conventions.md` branch-naming rules.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/scenarios/ssid-env-var-absent-fallback.md:41:- Backlog: `../backlogs/abort-mid-commit-partial-session.md` (related recovery-path coverage gap).
