.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:15:# Promote-now rollback semantics doc home
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:17:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:19:Design Decision D-3 (commit-on-branch for Preparation promote-now) includes a partial-failure rollback: if `git commit` fails post-copy, the manager must remove the copied skill file. The question was where to document this rollback sequence.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:21:## Question
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:23:Where should the promote-now rollback semantics live?
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:25:## Options considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:26:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:27:1. **preparation/SKILL.md** (recommended) — co-located with the narrow-exception text describing the promote-now procedure. Preserves single-source-of-truth.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:28:2. **git/SKILL.md** — alongside the general git critical-rule paragraph. Creates cross-skill indirection.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:30:## User decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:31:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:32:`preparation/SKILL.md` confirmed. Rollback semantics live co-located with the narrow-exception promote-now text.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:34:## Rollback sequence
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:35:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:36:1. `git commit` fails post-copy
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:37:2. Manager: `git -C "$worktreePath" rm <copied-paths>` — removes the copied skill file
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:38:3. Surface failure to user via AskUserQuestion
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:39:4. Re-attempt or abort per user response
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:40:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:41:**Critical**: rollback REMOVES the copied file (NOT `git checkout`). The file did not pre-exist in the worktree before the promote-now operation. `git checkout` would fail or restore to HEAD, which has no version of this file. Removal is the only correct recovery. See `decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md` for the formal decision record.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:42:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:43:## Implication
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:44:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:45:The Execution task implementing the promote-now commit-on-branch owns both the promote-now path and the rollback semantics documentation in `preparation/SKILL.md`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:46:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:47:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:48:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:49:- `decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md` — the formal decision record for the `git rm` (not `git checkout`) rollback.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md:50:- `design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md` — Design Decision D-3, the commit-on-branch path whose rollback this discussion places.
