.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/anchor-slug-4-hyphen-vs-2-hyphen.md:14:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/anchor-slug-4-hyphen-vs-2-hyphen.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/anchor-slug-4-hyphen-vs-2-hyphen.md:16:# Anchor slug format — 4-hyphen vs 2-hyphen for em-dash headings
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/anchor-slug-4-hyphen-vs-2-hyphen.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/anchor-slug-4-hyphen-vs-2-hyphen.md:18:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/anchor-slug-4-hyphen-vs-2-hyphen.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/anchor-slug-4-hyphen-vs-2-hyphen.md:20:The worktree-creation row in `orchestration/SKILL.md` links to `git/SKILL.md` via anchors `#p2----create-worktree` and `#p6----recover-orphaned-worktree`. The source headings are `### P2 — Create worktree` and `### P6 — Recover orphaned worktree`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/anchor-slug-4-hyphen-vs-2-hyphen.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/anchor-slug-4-hyphen-vs-2-hyphen.md:22:The project's stub-redirect-format rule (`rules/stub-redirect-format.md`) says em/en dashes are **dropped** for anchor verification — by that rule the expected slugs would be `p2--create-worktree` and `p6--recover-orphaned-worktree` (2 hyphens). The existing links use 4 hyphens, and the anchor format has not been empirically tested by rendering the markdown in GitHub.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/anchor-slug-4-hyphen-vs-2-hyphen.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/anchor-slug-4-hyphen-vs-2-hyphen.md:24:## Why deferred
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/anchor-slug-4-hyphen-vs-2-hyphen.md:25:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/anchor-slug-4-hyphen-vs-2-hyphen.md:26:Low priority and out of the originating task's contracted scope (which was the stale-path recovery and footnote-reference fixes only). Link navigation is cosmetic: the procedure text reads clearly whether or not the anchor resolves in a rendered context, and the 4-hyphen form already appears across the project. A correct fix requires a project-wide anchor sweep of all em-dash headings, which is not scoped to a single task.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/anchor-slug-4-hyphen-vs-2-hyphen.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/anchor-slug-4-hyphen-vs-2-hyphen.md:28:## When to pick up
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/anchor-slug-4-hyphen-vs-2-hyphen.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/anchor-slug-4-hyphen-vs-2-hyphen.md:30:Pick up when a dedicated docs-sweep task audits em-dash anchor slugs project-wide, or sooner if link resolution is confirmed broken by rendering the markdown in GitHub. No hard prerequisite.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/anchor-slug-4-hyphen-vs-2-hyphen.md:31:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/anchor-slug-4-hyphen-vs-2-hyphen.md:32:## Suggested approach
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/anchor-slug-4-hyphen-vs-2-hyphen.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/anchor-slug-4-hyphen-vs-2-hyphen.md:34:1. Render `orchestration/SKILL.md` in GitHub and confirm whether `#p2----create-worktree` / `#p6----recover-orphaned-worktree` resolve, or whether the 2-hyphen form is required.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/anchor-slug-4-hyphen-vs-2-hyphen.md:35:2. If the 2-hyphen form is correct, run a project-wide sweep of all em-dash-heading anchors and normalize them, updating both the stub-redirect-format rule's example and any links that depend on the resolved form.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/anchor-slug-4-hyphen-vs-2-hyphen.md:36:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/anchor-slug-4-hyphen-vs-2-hyphen.md:37:## Originating session
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/anchor-slug-4-hyphen-vs-2-hyphen.md:38:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/anchor-slug-4-hyphen-vs-2-hyphen.md:39:Surfaced by structural evaluation findings during the worktree-first session-architecture work (session `1b26cf20`, 2026-05-24). Full session detail: `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/direct-mode-retained-opt-out.md:1:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/direct-mode-retained-opt-out.md:2:name: direct-mode-retained-opt-out
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/direct-mode-retained-opt-out.md:3:description: Direct mode is preserved as a documented opt-out from worktree-first; users set settings.git.workflow.mode=direct to bypass worktree creation.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/direct-mode-retained-opt-out.md:4:type: design
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/direct-mode-retained-opt-out.md:5:scope: feature
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/direct-mode-retained-opt-out.md:6:feature: git-workflow
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/direct-mode-retained-opt-out.md:7:status: locked
