.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:1:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:2:name: flock-serialization-on-session-json
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:3:description: POSIX flock -x on session.json serializes concurrent PostToolUse hook and reconstructor read-modify-write cycles; lock released automatically on process exit.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:4:type: design
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:5:scope: feature
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:6:feature: install-runtime
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:7:status: locked
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:8:created: 2026-05-23
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:9:session: 1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:10:tags: [flock, serialization, session-json, concurrency]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:11:design-id: D-3-5
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:12:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:13:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:14:# Serialization primitive: POSIX flock -x on session.json
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:16:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:18:The PostToolUse hook and the reconstructor both perform read-modify-write cycles on `session.json`. When two Task tools are spawned in parallel (the dual-system evaluator pattern fires two hooks concurrently), both can read `session.json` before either writes — a lost-update race that drops one subagent's record. A serialization primitive was needed that is correct, minimal, and safe against abnormal process death.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:20:## Decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:22:Every read-modify-write cycle in both hook and reconstructor MUST:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:24:```bash
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:25:exec {fd}>>"$session_json"
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:26:flock -x "$fd"
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:27:# ... read, modify, write session.json atomically ...
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:28:# lock released automatically on script exit
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:29:```
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:31:`flock -x` on `session.json` itself (not a sidecar). Lock is released automatically when the script's process exits (POSIX `flock(2)` semantics — releases on process death, including SIGKILL).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:32:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:33:**Sidecar refinement**: using `session.json.lock` as a dedicated sidecar would be cleaner separation, but is deferred as non-blocking hardening (see backlog: `sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred`).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:34:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:35:## Rationale
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:36:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:37:Concurrent PostToolUse hooks (e.g., dual-system evaluator spawns) cause lost-update race when both read `session.json` before either writes. Three options considered: (a) `flock -x`, (b) per-spawn file pattern, (c) accept lost-update. Picked **(a)** because: smallest change (one `exec {fd}>>"$session_json"` line per script); serializes both hook AND reconstructor; no consolidation step.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:38:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:39:Supporting evidence anchored at decision time: the first-iteration evaluation finding (the concurrent-hook race); the parallel evaluator topology documented in `delegation/SKILL.md` (the dual-system pattern that triggers concurrent hooks); and `session-start.sh` (the bash precedent plus host-capability confirmation that flock is available).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:40:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:41:## Alternatives considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:42:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:43:- (b) Per-spawn files — rejected: adds a consolidation step plus cross-file ordering semantics; data lives in N files until Wrap-up consolidates, breaking real-time `session.json` reads.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:44:- (c) Accept lost-update — rejected: defeats the reconstructor's premise; running the reconstructor at every Task return is wasteful and the same race re-occurs between the reconstructor and a concurrent hook.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:45:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:46:## Consequences
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:47:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:48:- Both the hook script and the reconstructor script must wrap every read-modify-write cycle in the `flock -x` block above; documentation for both scripts must state the requirement.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:49:- A cleaner `session.json.lock` sidecar refinement is deferred as non-blocking hardening (backlog `sidecar-lock-refinement-deferred`).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:50:- Validation obligations: a parallel-spawn smoke test (spawn two Task tools; `jq '.agents | length'` returns N+2, not N+1 or N) and a lock-release-on-exit test (`kill -9` a hook process mid-run; the next hook fire acquires the lock cleanly).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:51:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:52:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:53:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:54:- `hook-bash-jq-stack.md` — the authoring stack whose read step this serialization protects.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:55:- `reconstructor-verify-and-fix.md` — the reconstructor whose read-modify-write cycle is the other side of the race.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:56:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/install-runtime/design/flock-serialization-on-session-json.md:57:## Source
