.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:12:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:13:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:14:# Commit-on-branch for Preparation promote-now (D-3)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:16:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:18:`preparation/SKILL.md` has a narrow exception that allows a skill to be generated and copied into the worktree during Preparation (the "promote-now" path). Before this design, that path copied the generated skill body but did not commit it, leaving the artifact outside worktree-first history until some later commit happened to pick it up. The open question was whether the promote-now path should close itself by committing the generated artifact to the worktree branch, and how to recover if that commit fails after the copy.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:20:## Decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:22:Extend `preparation/SKILL.md` narrow-exception promote-now path to run a worktree-branch commit as its closing step:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:24:```
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:25:git -C "$worktreePath" add <promoted-files>
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:26:git -C "$worktreePath" commit \
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:27:  -m "chore(skills): promote {slug} generated by preparation iter{n}" \
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:28:  -m "AI-Provenance-Record: gobbi://session/{session-id}/task/preparation-promote-now-iter{n}"
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:29:```
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:31:**Partial-failure rollback**: if `git commit` fails post-copy, manager MUST `git -C "$worktreePath" rm` the copied file and surface to user via AskUserQuestion before re-attempt.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:32:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:33:## Rationale
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:34:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:35:The Preparation promote-now path (narrow exception allowing skill generation during Preparation) was already a sole-writer deviation; commit-on-branch is the structural completion that ties the generated artifact into worktree-first history. The `-C "$worktreePath"` flag is explicit about which tree receives the commit. The canonical `AI-Provenance-Record` trailer form is `gobbi://session/{session-id}/task/{task-id}` per `git/conventions.md`. The rollback mechanism (git rm after failed commit) addresses the partial-promotion failure mode where a copied file must be removed if the commit cannot complete.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:36:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:37:## Alternatives considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:38:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:39:- **`feat(skills):` subject** — rejected: the skill is generated by workflow automation, not authored as a user-facing product feature, so `chore(skills):` is the honest type.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:40:- **An alternative `AI-Provenance-Record` trailer form** — rejected: a new trailer shape would require a separate Scope Contract item; the current `gobbi://session/{session-id}/task/{task-id}` slot is expressive enough to identify the promote-now operation.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:41:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:42:## Consequences
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:43:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:44:The promote-now path now ends in a worktree-branch commit, tying the generated skill into worktree-first history. Any executor implementing this path must include the partial-failure rollback (`git rm` the copied file on commit failure, then AskUserQuestion) — see `decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md` for why `git rm` (not `git checkout`) is the only correct recovery. Verification: a future-session smoke test confirms `git log --oneline` for the next `generate-now` shows a subject matching `^chore\(skills\): promote .*` with a body containing `AI-Provenance-Record: gobbi://session/[a-f0-9-]+/task/preparation-promote-now-iter[0-9]+`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:45:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:46:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:47:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:48:- `decisions/2026-05-24-rollback-semantics-drift-from-ideation.md` — the rollback correction (`git rm`, not `git checkout`) for this path's partial-failure case.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:49:- `discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md` — where the rollback semantics are documented (`preparation/SKILL.md`).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:50:- `discussions/promote-now-depends-on-worktree-first.md` — the discussion confirming this path depends on worktree-first.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:51:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:52:## Source
