.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:9:session: 1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:10:tags: [git-workflow, worktree-first, architecture, collapsing-strategies]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:11:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:12:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:13:# Worktree-first vs alternative collapsing strategies — worktree-first locked
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:14:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:15:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:16:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:17:The session set out to fix the artifact-misroute failure mode (session writes landing in the main tree instead of the worktree). Three architectural strategies could collapse the two surfaces (main tree + worktree) into a coherent session layout, and the session had to choose one before any downstream design decision could be made.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:18:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:19:## Question
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:20:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:21:Should the session architecture use worktree-first, two-surface, or symlink-into-worktree?
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:22:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:23:## Options considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:24:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:25:1. **Worktree-first** (recommended) — the session directory lives in the worktree tree from session start; all writes root at `worktreePath`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:26:2. **Two-surface** — one main-tree session dir plus one worktree for generated files; the two surfaces are kept separate.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:27:3. **Symlink-into-worktree** — the session dir stays in the main tree and is symlinked into the worktree.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:28:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:29:## User decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:30:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:31:User locked **worktree-first**. The two-surface and symlink-into-worktree alternatives were deferred to backlog items for future evaluation rather than rejected outright.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:32:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:33:## Implication
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:34:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:35:Every subsequent design decision for the git-workflow feature assumes the session directory lives in the worktree tree. The two alternatives remain as backlog candidates if future evidence motivates revisiting.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:36:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:37:## Related
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:38:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:39:- `design/worktree-create-before-session-stamp.md` — the worktree-creation step (D-1) that implements the chosen worktree-first strategy.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/worktree-first-vs-collapsing-strategies.md:40:- `discussions/session-memory-survival.md` — the follow-on discussion on how worktree-resident session memory survives.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:1:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:2:name: lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:3:description: T1→T3 wave ordering was stated in prose only, not machine-enforced in the task dependency graph — decision to add graph edges.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:4:type: decisions
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:5:scope: feature
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:6:feature: workflow
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:7:status: accepted
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:8:created: 2026-05-24
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:9:session: 1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:10:tags: [planning, wave-ordering, dependency-graph, lock1]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:11:domain: structure
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:12:supersedes: null
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:13:decision_status: accepted
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:14:---
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:15:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:16:# Wave ordering not graph-enforced — T1→T3 dependency edges added
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:17:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:18:## Context
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:19:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:20:The first Planning draft stated in prose that the T1 wave (Tasks 01-06) must complete before the T3 wave (Tasks 07-10). However, Task 07's `requires:` field only listed `[05]`, which permitted Task 06 to run in parallel with or after Task 07 — violating the stated wave gate. Additionally, Tasks 06 and 10 both touch `orchestration/SKILL.md` with no ordering edge between them.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:22:## Decision
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:24:Add the missing dependency-graph edges so the wave gate is machine-enforced:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:25:- Task 07 `requires` changed from `[05]` to `[05, 06]`, graph-enforcing both terminal T1 wave leaves as prerequisites.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:26:- Task 10 `requires` gains `06`, enforcing the `orchestration/SKILL.md` sequential-edit ordering.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:27:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:28:## Rationale
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:29:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:30:The prose claim "the T1 wave completes before the T3 wave starts" must be machine-readable in the task graph, not just prose. With only `requires: [05]`, a scheduler or manager could legitimately start Task 07 while Task 06 was still in progress. The strengthened edges close this loophole. Both 05 AND 06 are required on Task 07 because 05 brings the phase-docs cadence rule and 06 brings the direct-mode opt-out, both T1 surfaces the T3 hook script must respect.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:31:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:32:## Alternatives considered
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:33:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:34:- **Leave the wave gate as prose with `requires: [05]`.** Rejected: prose ordering is not enforced by the scheduler, and the single `[05]` prerequisite let Task 06 race Task 07.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:35:- **Gate Task 07 on Task 05 only.** Rejected: that omits the direct-mode opt-out brought by Task 06, which the hook script depends on; both terminal leaves must gate the T3 wave.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:36:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:37:## Consequences
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:38:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:39:The execution order is now strictly 01 → 02 → 03 → 04 → 05 → 06 → 07 → 08 → 09 → 10 (Task 09 may run before 08, since 09 depends only on 07). No T3 task can begin before both 05 and 06 complete.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:40:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/workflow/decisions/2026-05-24-lock1-wave-ordering-not-graph-enforced.md:41:## Related
