.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/chore-label-line-citation-stale.md:20:The design drafts for the worktree-first session architecture cited "`chore | #e4e669` at line 261" in `git/conventions.md`. A Codex evaluator ran `grep -n` and found `fix` at line 261; `chore` is at line 263.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/chore-label-line-citation-stale.md:21:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/chore-label-line-citation-stale.md:22:The branch name `chore/session-{date}-{ssid-short}` is correctly registry-compliant — the label exists at line 263 and the type regex at line 22 includes `chore`. This is a citation-accuracy issue only.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/chore-label-line-citation-stale.md:23:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/chore-label-line-citation-stale.md:24:## Why deferred
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/chore-label-line-citation-stale.md:25:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/chore-label-line-citation-stale.md:26:A Low-priority docs-sync finding only — the off-by-2 citation affects no runtime behavior or design decision. The branch-convention compliance was verified independently (type regex at line 22 includes `chore`, slug length at line 64 passes, and the `chore` label is confirmed present at line 263), so the stale citation is purely a documentation-accuracy nit not worth blocking the current workflow step.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/backlogs/chore-label-line-citation-stale.md:27:
